  ('acne-treatment', 'gurgaon', false, false, null, 'Acne treatment in Gurgaon (Gurugram): course cost, visits, side effects, and how to plan follow-ups. Reviewed by a registered doctor.', null, null, null, null, null, null, null, true, null, null, '{"followups":"varies","aftercare":"varies"}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"A partner facility exists in Gurgaon for other treatments, and whether it runs dermatology is to be confirmed. We do not name it. Acne care here would be a dermatology clinic or an outpatient department, and the checks below apply to either.","partners":[{"type":"Dermatology clinic or hospital outpatient department in Gurgaon (to be confirmed)","count":null}],"accreditation":null,"checks":[{"check":"Doctor registration","why":"Acne tablets and procedures should be directed by a registered dermatologist","ask":"Which council is the doctor registered with, and where can I check it?"},{"check":"Evening or early slots","why":"Reviews recur, so slot times decide whether you keep them","ask":"Which times are available for follow-ups, and can they be fixed?"},{"check":"Written plan with visits","why":"Acne is a course, so the number of visits matters","ask":"How many reviews are in the quote, and what is an extra one?"},{"check":"Who does the procedure","why":"Peels and light sessions need training and clean tools","ask":"Who performs it, and how are tools cleaned?"},{"check":"Pregnancy and tablet rules","why":"Some tablets need tests and an agreed pregnancy plan","ask":"What do you need from me before tablets, and how often are checks?"}]}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"Gurgaon visits are usually squeezed between work and the commute, so the useful question is how close the clinic is to your office or home and at what hour you can go.","airport":"Indira Gandhi International Airport, Delhi (to be verified)","station":"HUDA City Centre (Yellow Line) and Sikandarpur (Rapid Metro)","stayDays":"Same day. No stay for consultations and reviews","metro":"Sikandarpur and HUDA City Centre stations serve much of the commercial belt, and many people walk or take a short cab from there. {sample} Station distance to a facility is added once one is confirmed.","roadTimes":[{"from":"South Delhi","time":"40 to 70 min","tip":"Pick a slot before the evening rush on the highway"},{"from":"Noida","time":"70 to 110 min","tip":"Ask whether video reviews are possible between in-person visits"},{"from":"Faridabad","time":"60 to 100 min","tip":"A fixed weekend or early slot is easier to keep"},{"from":"Rewari","time":"60 to 90 min","tip":"Combine the visit with other work in the city"}],"privacyNote":"Many people here work in offices where colleagues notice time off. You do not have to explain a visit to anyone. Ask the clinic not to print the treatment name on any message it sends.","mapCaption":"Travel into Gurgaon from Delhi and nearby towns, no building shown."}'::jsonb, '[{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: whether the Gurgaon partner facility runs a dermatology service, and its type","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: groundwater quality for Gurugram (Central Ground Water Board report, year)","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: seasonal air quality in Gurugram (public CPCB records)","source":"","asOf":""}]'::jsonb, 'For people in Gurgaon (Gurugram) and the NCR who commute daily and need an acne plan that survives a work schedule, with notes on slots, offices and monsoon travel.', '{}'::jsonb, false, '[]'::jsonb, '["Many people in Gurgaon fit acne reviews around office hours and a long commute.","Ask which follow-ups can be a video call and which need an in-person look.","Monsoon waterlogging can turn a short drive into a long one, so book reviews with spare time."]'::jsonb, null, '[{"heading":"Gurgaon or Gurugram","text":"They are the same city. We use Gurgaon here because more people search for it, and the body text also says Gurugram. Either spelling works when you ask a clinic."},{"heading":"Slots around work","text":"Ask which weekdays and hours are held for follow-ups. A short review before or after work is easier to keep than one in the middle of the day. Say so before you start, not after you have missed two."},{"heading":"Air-conditioned offices","text":"Long hours in an air-conditioned office can leave skin dry, and acne creams add to that. Mention it at the review, because the doctor may adjust how often you use the cream or suggest a moisturiser."},{"heading":"Coming from Delhi or beyond","text":"People travel here from South Delhi, Noida, Faridabad and Rewari. Decide at the start who sees you between visits if you live far from the clinic, and keep the one-page plan on your phone."}]'::jsonb, 'Acne Treatment in Gurgaon: Cost, Timeline, Risks', 'Acne treatment in Gurgaon', 'Acne treatment in Gurgaon (also written Gurugram) means a consultation and then repeat visits for months. The local price range is {tbc} until quotes are collected. Many people fit visits around office hours, so ask about early or late slots and whether some reviews can be by video.', '[{"heading":"Plans that survive a work schedule","paragraphs":["A plan for acne asks for steady use of creams and a visit every few weeks. In Gurgaon the limit is rarely interest, it is time. Many people begin with enthusiasm and miss the third review. Ask at the start how long the early visits take and whether the doctor can keep slots free before or after normal hours.","If your plan includes tablets, the doctor may ask for blood tests before and during the course. Ask whether those can be done at a lab near your office and sent to the clinic, so one visit does not turn into three."]},{"heading":"Heat, sweat and the long summer","paragraphs":["Summers in Gurgaon run from April into September and are hot and sweaty. Heat and sun can darken acne marks, and some medicines make skin burn more easily. Ask your doctor which sun protection suits you and how to adjust in the hot months.","Peels and light sessions are often planned for cooler months because redness and flaking fit poorly with strong sun. The doctor decides that for your skin type. Do not book a procedure just before a trip."]},{"heading":"Water and what the tap does to skin","paragraphs":["Groundwater in parts of Gurugram is reported to be hard or salty, and many homes use filters. We do not claim that this causes acne. If your skin feels tight and flaky after washing, tell the doctor, who can suggest a gentler wash. Avoid adding scrubs."]},{"heading":"Language and referral habits","paragraphs":["Hindi and English are the working languages of most clinics here, and the first call can be in either. Some patients arrive after a family doctor or a chemist suggested a skin specialist. Bring any note from them, and a list of what you have used.","Ask the clinic for your plan in writing, with the dates of your next two reviews, and keep them in your phone calendar."]},{"heading":"Monsoon and travel","paragraphs":["Heavy rain can cause waterlogging on roads here and long delays. Leave extra time in July and August, and ask whether a short missed review can move by a day. A review delayed by a week rarely matters, but a skipped course can."]}]'::jsonb),
  ('acne-treatment', 'delhi', false, false, null, 'Acne treatment in Delhi: what a course costs, how many visits, side effects, and travel and follow-up planning from nearby towns.', null, null, null, null, null, null, null, true, null, null, '{"followups":"varies","aftercare":"varies"}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"No partner facility is confirmed in Delhi yet. Acne care is usually a dermatology clinic or a hospital outpatient department, and this page will say which once it is known. Until then, run the checks below on any place you are given.","partners":[{"type":"Dermatology clinic or hospital outpatient department in Delhi (to be confirmed)","count":null}],"accreditation":null,"checks":[{"check":"Doctor registration","why":"Acne tablets and procedures should be directed by a registered dermatologist","ask":"Which council is the doctor registered with, and can I check it on the public register?"},{"check":"Examination before any plan","why":"A plan made from a photo misses things a doctor sees in person","ask":"Will the doctor examine my skin at the first visit?"},{"check":"Written plan with visits","why":"Acne is a course, so the number of visits matters","ask":"How many reviews are in the quote, and what is an extra one?"},{"check":"Who does the procedure","why":"Peels and light sessions need training and clean tools","ask":"Who performs it, and how are tools and tips cleaned?"},{"check":"Pregnancy and tablet rules","why":"Some tablets need tests and an agreed pregnancy plan","ask":"What do you need from me before tablets, and how often are checks?"}]}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"Acne follow-ups are short and frequent, so a clinic near your office or a metro line matters more than anything else. Ask for a mid-morning or early-afternoon slot.","airport":"Indira Gandhi International Airport (to be verified)","station":"New Delhi, Old Delhi and Hazrat Nizamuddin stations (to be verified against the facility)","stayDays":"Same day. No stay for consultations and reviews","metro":"Most reviews are easy by metro. After a peel, skin can be red and sensitive to sun and dust, so a cab or a cover-up helps. {sample} The nearest station is added once a facility is confirmed.","roadTimes":[{"from":"Noida","time":"50 to 90 min","tip":"Book the review before the evening peak"},{"from":"Ghaziabad","time":"60 to 100 min","tip":"Ask whether some reviews can be a video call with photos"},{"from":"Faridabad","time":"50 to 90 min","tip":"Keep a fixed weekday slot so the visit becomes routine"},{"from":"Gurgaon","time":"50 to 90 min","tip":"Leave before the morning peak or after 11"}],"privacyNote":"Photos of your skin are health data. Ask where clinic photos are stored and who can see them. No building name is printed on messages we send.","mapCaption":"Travel into Delhi from nearby towns, no building shown."}'::jsonb, '[{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: which Delhi facility, if any, will provide acne care","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: winter and post-Diwali air quality in Delhi (public CPCB records, month and station)","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: tap water quality by area of Delhi (public water board reports)","source":"","asOf":""}]'::jsonb, 'For readers who live in Delhi or the nearby NCR towns and plan months of follow-ups around traffic, winter air and wedding-season dates. It gives local planning points, not a clinic recommendation.', '{}'::jsonb, false, '[]'::jsonb, '["In Delhi, traffic more than distance decides how easy review visits are.","Wedding season fills the winter months, so start a plan well before an event.","Ask whether clinic photos of your skin stay with the clinic."]'::jsonb, null, '[{"heading":"Choosing a slot","text":"Review visits are short. Mid-morning and early afternoon on weekdays are the quietest hours on Delhi roads, and a fixed weekly or fortnightly slot is easier to keep than a different time every visit."},{"heading":"Bring your history","text":"Many people begin with a chemist or a family doctor before seeing a dermatologist. Bring the names of creams you have used and for how long. A chemist can sell a cream, but only a doctor can prescribe tablets."},{"heading":"Parents of teenagers","text":"A parent usually comes to the first visit. Ask the doctor to explain the plan to the teenager and the parent together, and to write the visit dates down."},{"heading":"A written plan for a local doctor","text":"Ask for a one-page plan that a doctor in Noida, Faridabad or Ghaziabad could follow if a review is missed. The coordinator can check what a local doctor may change and what needs your dermatologist."}]'::jsonb, 'Acne Treatment in Delhi: Cost, Timeline, Risks', 'Acne treatment in Delhi', 'Acne treatment in Delhi is a course of visits over months, not one appointment. Expect a first consultation and then reviews every few weeks. The local price range is {tbc} until quotes are collected. In Delhi, traffic more than distance decides how easy those visits are.', '[{"heading":"How a course fits into a Delhi week","paragraphs":["A plan for acne asks for a visit every few weeks for months. That is the real commitment, more than the price of any one visit. In Delhi the time a visit takes is set by the road, so choose a clinic by how easily you can reach it on a regular working day.","Ask at the first visit which reviews need you in person and which could be a short video call with photos. Skin is hard to judge on a screen, so the doctor may still want to see it at certain points, especially when tablets or a peel are involved."]},{"heading":"Winter air, dust and your skin","paragraphs":["Air quality in Delhi is at its worst in the weeks after Diwali and through much of winter, and winter air is also dry. Many people ask whether pollution causes their acne. We do not claim that it does, and no page can say so for one person. A dermatologist may talk about gentle cleansing, how dry air interacts with acne creams, and sun protection in summer.","Creams that dry the skin can sting more in winter. Ask which moisturiser suits your plan and whether the routine should change between seasons. Report burning or swelling early."]},{"heading":"Water, washing and what not to add","paragraphs":["Tap water in parts of Delhi is described as hard, and some people feel their skin gets tight after washing. There is no basis here to blame water for acne. If your skin feels dry after washing, mention it. The doctor may suggest a different cleanser, and that is better than adding scrubs or extra products on your own."]},{"heading":"Language and who to ask first","paragraphs":["Consultations in Hindi and English are normal in Delhi, and some clinics also speak Punjabi. Ask for the written plan in the language you read most easily. {tbc}","A family doctor can refer you and send notes about earlier treatment. That helps the dermatologist see what has been tried. If you were prescribed tablets before, tell the doctor how long you took them and why you stopped."]},{"heading":"Timing around exams and weddings","paragraphs":["Wedding season runs through the winter months, and board exams fall in early spring. Both bring stress and a wish for quick change. Start a plan at least two to three months before an event, and avoid starting a peel in the last weeks, since early weeks can bring dryness or a flare. Ask the doctor what is realistic for your date."]}]'::jsonb),
  ('acne-treatment', 'lucknow', false, false, null, 'Acne treatment in Lucknow: what a course costs, how often you return, side effects, and travel from Barabanki, Unnao and Sitapur.', null, null, null, null, null, null, null, true, null, null, '{"followups":"varies","aftercare":"varies"}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"No partner facility is confirmed in Lucknow yet. Acne care here would be a dermatology clinic or a hospital outpatient department. If care ends up in another city we will say so at the top of this page and not claim a local site.","partners":[{"type":"Dermatology clinic or hospital outpatient department in Lucknow (to be confirmed)","count":null}],"accreditation":null,"checks":[{"check":"Doctor registration","why":"Acne tablets and procedures should be directed by a registered dermatologist","ask":"Which council is the doctor registered with, and where can I check it?"},{"check":"Plan a local doctor can follow","why":"Patients from small towns cannot return every month","ask":"Can the plan be written so a doctor near my home can follow it?"},{"check":"Written plan with visits","why":"Acne is a course, so the number of visits matters","ask":"How many reviews are in the quote, and what is an extra one?"},{"check":"Who does the procedure","why":"Peels and light sessions need training and clean tools","ask":"Who performs it, and how are tools cleaned?"},{"check":"Pregnancy and tablet rules","why":"Some tablets need tests and an agreed pregnancy plan","ask":"What do you need from me before tablets, and how often are checks?"}]}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"Many people who ask about acne treatment in Lucknow live in a nearby district and come in by road or train. The plan runs more smoothly when each trip has a purpose and the gaps between trips are covered locally.","airport":"Chaudhary Charan Singh International Airport, Lucknow (to be verified)","station":"Charbagh station and the Lucknow Metro (to be verified against the facility)","stayDays":"Same day for most visits. No stay for consultations and reviews","metro":"The Lucknow Metro runs along a north-south line and is useful for a consultation in the city. After a peel, a cab with the window up keeps dust and sun off the skin. {sample} Station names near a facility are added once it is confirmed.","roadTimes":[{"from":"Barabanki","time":"40 to 70 min","tip":"Short enough for a same-day review"},{"from":"Unnao","time":"60 to 100 min","tip":"Book the early review slot to avoid afternoon heat"},{"from":"Sitapur","time":"80 to 120 min","tip":"Ask which reviews can be done by video or locally"},{"from":"Hardoi","time":"100 to 150 min","tip":"Combine the visit with other errands in the city"}],"privacyNote":"In smaller towns a neighbour may recognise you at a clinic. A quiet slot or a different waiting area can help, and you can ask the clinic not to name the treatment on messages.","mapCaption":"Travel into Lucknow from nearby districts, no building shown."}'::jsonb, '[{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: which Lucknow facility, if any, will provide acne care","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: road times from Barabanki, Unnao, Sitapur and Hardoi, checked on a map with a date","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: Lucknow climate normals for heat, humidity and fog (IMD)","source":"","asOf":""}]'::jsonb, 'For readers in Lucknow and the surrounding districts who must plan repeated trips for acne care, with notes on follow-up by road, summer heat, winter fog and who can review between visits.', '{}'::jsonb, false, '[]'::jsonb, '["From a district town, the question is who sees your skin between the Lucknow visits.","Summer in Lucknow is hot and dry, and the monsoon is humid, and both affect how skin feels under creams.","A written plan that a local doctor can follow keeps a course going when a trip is missed."]'::jsonb, null, '[{"heading":"Who checks you between visits","text":"Ask the dermatologist which changes a local doctor may make and which need a call to the clinic. Write down the clinic''s number and the dates of your next two reviews before you leave."},{"heading":"Coming from a district town","text":"A review needs one early trip in and one ride home. Barabanki can be a same-day visit. From Sitapur or Hardoi, plan the whole day and bring water and a cap or umbrella, since skin on some creams burns more easily in sun."},{"heading":"Hindi and Awadhi speakers","text":"The consultation can be in Hindi or Hinglish. If words in a leaflet are hard, ask the clinic to explain them aloud and to write the plan in a language you read easily. {tbc}"},{"heading":"Marriages and festivals","text":"Roads and hotels fill during wedding season and around Diwali and Eid. Book reviews early in those weeks, and avoid starting a peel just before a family event."}]'::jsonb, 'Acne Treatment in Lucknow: Cost, Timeline, Risks', 'Acne treatment in Lucknow', 'Acne treatment in Lucknow means a first consultation and then reviews every few weeks for months. The local price range is {tbc} until quotes are collected. If you live in a nearby town, plan the visits and who sees you between them before you start.', '[{"heading":"Planning visits from outside the city","paragraphs":["A course of acne treatment is a string of short visits, and for a patient from Unnao or Sitapur each visit is most of a day. Before you start, work out how many trips are realistic and tell the doctor. A plan built around four visits can differ from a plan built around twelve.","Ask whether early reviews can be by video, with photos taken in daylight, and whether blood tests, if needed, can be done at a lab near home and sent on. The doctor will say what can and cannot be done remotely."]},{"heading":"Hot dry summers, humid monsoon, foggy winters","paragraphs":["Lucknow summers are hot and dry, the monsoon is humid, and winter mornings can be foggy. Heat and sweat make some creams feel heavy. Dry months make others sting. Ask whether to change your routine in May and June and what to do in the humid weeks.","Strong sun can darken marks left by acne and make some medicines sting more. The doctor will tell you what protection fits your plan."]},{"heading":"Water from the Gomti and the tap","paragraphs":["Households here use a mix of piped supply and groundwater, and hardness varies by area. We do not claim that water causes acne. If skin feels tight after washing, mention it at the next review and let the doctor choose the cleanser."]},{"heading":"Referral habits and being heard","paragraphs":["In smaller towns many people start with a local doctor or a medical shop and arrive in Lucknow after months of trying creams. That history helps. Bring the packets or photographs of the labels, and tell the doctor how long you used each.","If you are told you need tablets, ask for the plan in writing, including the tests and the dates of review. Do not buy tablets without a prescription or share them with family."]},{"heading":"Seasonal timing","paragraphs":["Peels and light sessions create redness and flaking that fit badly with strong summer sun. Doctors often plan them for cooler months, and your doctor will say if that applies to you. Start any plan well before a wedding, and tell the doctor the date."]}]'::jsonb),
  ('acne-treatment', 'kanpur', false, false, null, 'Acne treatment in Kanpur: course cost, number of visits, side effects, and follow-up planning for patients from Unnao and nearby towns.', null, null, null, null, null, null, null, true, null, null, '{"followups":"varies","aftercare":"varies"}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"No partner facility is confirmed in Kanpur, and Lucknow is the nearest other city we cover. If care is in Lucknow we will say so at the top of this page and give the trip time. Until then this page shows how a plan is made and what to check.","partners":[{"type":"Dermatology clinic or hospital outpatient department in Kanpur (to be confirmed)","count":null}],"accreditation":null,"checks":[{"check":"Doctor registration","why":"Acne tablets and procedures should be directed by a registered dermatologist","ask":"Which council is the doctor registered with, and where can I check it?"},{"check":"Where reviews happen","why":"A review in Lucknow means a longer trip than one in Kanpur","ask":"Can the early reviews be in Kanpur and only the procedures elsewhere?"},{"check":"Written plan with visits","why":"Acne is a course, so the number of visits matters","ask":"How many reviews are in the quote, and what is an extra one?"},{"check":"Who does the procedure","why":"Peels and light sessions need training and clean tools","ask":"Who performs it, and how are tools cleaned?"},{"check":"Pregnancy and tablet rules","why":"Some tablets need tests and an agreed pregnancy plan","ask":"What do you need from me before tablets, and how often are checks?"}]}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"For acne, the Kanpur question is simple: can most reviews be in Kanpur, and which, if any, need a trip to Lucknow. Settle that before you start.","airport":"Kanpur civil airport and Lucknow airport (service and schedules to be verified)","station":"Kanpur Central, and Charbagh in Lucknow (to be verified)","stayDays":"Same day for Kanpur visits. A Lucknow visit is a day trip","metro":"Kanpur has a metro line that is partly open, and the part open and the route are to be checked against any facility. {sample} After a peel, a cab is easier on the skin than a crowded vehicle.","roadTimes":[{"from":"Unnao","time":"30 to 60 min","tip":"Close enough for a same-day review"},{"from":"Kanpur Dehat","time":"40 to 80 min","tip":"An early slot avoids afternoon heat"},{"from":"Fatehpur","time":"70 to 110 min","tip":"Ask for a longer gap between reviews if the doctor agrees"},{"from":"Lucknow","time":"100 to 150 min","tip":"The other city we cover. Compare the trip before you book"}],"privacyNote":"In a mid-sized city many people know each other. A quiet slot and discreet messages are reasonable requests, and the clinic should not print the treatment on any message.","mapCaption":"Travel into Kanpur from nearby towns, and the road to Lucknow, no building shown."}'::jsonb, '[{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: whether any partner facility exists in Kanpur for dermatology","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: Kanpur road time to Lucknow, from a map with a date","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: Kanpur air quality record (public CPCB station data) and tap water quality","source":"","asOf":""}]'::jsonb, 'For readers in Kanpur and nearby towns weighing whether to treat acne locally or travel to Lucknow, with notes on follow-up trips, industrial dust questions and cold winters.', '{}'::jsonb, false, '[]'::jsonb, '["The first question in Kanpur is whether follow-ups happen in Kanpur or need a trip to Lucknow.","Kanpur is an industrial city and people ask about dust. No claim is made that it causes acne.","A dermatologist in another city can write a plan a Kanpur doctor can follow."]'::jsonb, null, '[{"heading":"Kanpur or Lucknow","text":"If the first visit is in Lucknow, ask whether later reviews can be in Kanpur, with the plan shared by letter or phone. Many acne plans need the dermatologist''s eye only at a few points."},{"heading":"Dust and industrial air","text":"Kanpur is known as an industrial city, and people ask whether dust affects their skin. Whether it matters for your acne is a question for the reviewing dermatologist. We make no claim here. {pending}"},{"heading":"Winter cold and dry months","text":"Winters here are cold and dry, which can make acne creams harsher. Say so at the review so the doctor can adjust the routine, and ask about a moisturiser."},{"heading":"Language","text":"Hindi and Hinglish are common in clinics. Ask for the written plan in the language you read most easily, and for the names of medicines spelled out in a way you can show a local chemist."}]'::jsonb, 'Acne Treatment in Kanpur: Cost, Timeline, Risks', 'Acne treatment in Kanpur', 'Acne treatment in Kanpur is a course of visits over months. The local price range is {tbc} until quotes are collected. No partner facility is confirmed in Kanpur yet, so this page also covers the choice between Kanpur and Lucknow and what that means for repeat visits.', '[{"heading":"Do I have to go to Lucknow?","paragraphs":["That depends on whether a facility in Kanpur provides acne care, and none is confirmed yet. If a plan is made in Lucknow, the useful question is how often you must return. A good plan uses the specialist where the specialist is needed and a local doctor for simple reviews.","Ask how many visits are for procedures, such as peels, and how many are simple checks. Peels need to be done where the equipment and trained staff are. Cream reviews often can be shared with a Kanpur doctor if the plan is written down."]},{"heading":"Planning the gaps between visits","paragraphs":["A course is only as good as the weeks between visits. Decide before the first appointment who you will see if the skin burns, a spot grows or a rash appears. Write the name of that local doctor on the plan.","Keep a note of what you apply each day, and take photographs at the same time of day in the same light once a month. Both help a doctor who is not the one who wrote the plan."]},{"heading":"Cold winters and hot, dusty summers","paragraphs":["Kanpur has cold winters and hot summers. Cold air dries skin and acne creams can sting more, while summer heat and dust bring sweat and a wish to wash often. Washing too often can irritate acne-prone skin, so ask the doctor how often is right for you."]},{"heading":"Water and washing","paragraphs":["Water supply in the city mixes the river, piped supply and groundwater, and hardness differs by neighbourhood. We do not claim that water causes acne. If skin feels tight after washing, tell the doctor, and avoid adding scrubs or home remedies."]},{"heading":"Seasonal timing and travel","paragraphs":["Winter fog can delay trains and road trips to Lucknow. Book winter reviews with spare time, and avoid a long trip straight after a peel, when skin is red and sensitive. Ask the clinic to hold a same-day slot for your return trip if the road is slow."]}]'::jsonb),
  ('hydrafacial', 'gurgaon', false, false, null, 'Hydrafacial in Gurgaon (Gurugram): session cost, downtime, who should skip it, and how to compare quotes.', null, null, null, null, null, null, null, true, null, null, '{"review":"varies","aftercare":"varies"}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"A partner facility exists in Gurgaon for other treatments, and whether it provides skin-care sessions is to be confirmed. We do not name it. Sessions in this city are given in skin clinics, hospital skin departments and salons, so ask what kind of place you are in.","partners":[{"type":"Skin clinic or dermatology clinic in Gurgaon (to be confirmed)","count":null}],"accreditation":null,"checks":[{"check":"Who performs the session","why":"A doctor, a nurse and a technician have different training","ask":"Who will perform my session, and can I see their training?"},{"check":"Skin check first","why":"Active infection or sunburn means you should wait","ask":"Will someone look at my skin and ask about my medicines before starting?"},{"check":"Tips and tools","why":"Reused tools can spread infection","ask":"Are the tips single-use or cleaned, and how?"},{"check":"Serum and booster list","why":"Add-ons change the bill and can cause reactions","ask":"What is in the base price and what is extra?"},{"check":"Pack pressure","why":"Prepaid packs are hard to refund","ask":"Can I pay for one session first and decide on a pack afterwards?"}]}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"Most people in Gurgaon fit a session into a working day. The question is how close a clinic is to your office or home and whether the slot fits before the evening rush.","airport":"Indira Gandhi International Airport, Delhi (to be verified)","station":"HUDA City Centre (Yellow Line) and Sikandarpur (Rapid Metro)","stayDays":"Same day. No stay needed","metro":"Sikandarpur and HUDA City Centre serve much of the commercial belt. With pink skin, a short cab from the station is easier than a walk in the sun. {sample} The distance to a facility is added once one is confirmed.","roadTimes":[{"from":"South Delhi","time":"40 to 70 min","tip":"A mid-morning slot avoids the highway rush"},{"from":"Noida","time":"70 to 110 min","tip":"Check clinics in Noida before you travel for a short session"},{"from":"Faridabad","time":"60 to 100 min","tip":"A weekend slot is easier than a weekday one"},{"from":"Rewari","time":"60 to 90 min","tip":"Combine the visit with errands in the city"}],"privacyNote":"Many clients come from nearby offices. A short session need not be explained to colleagues. Ask the clinic not to name the session on messages and reminders.","mapCaption":"Travel into Gurgaon from Delhi and nearby towns, no building shown."}'::jsonb, '[{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: whether the Gurgaon partner facility provides skin-care sessions, and its type","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: groundwater quality for Gurugram (Central Ground Water Board report, year)","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: seasonal air quality in Gurugram (public CPCB records)","source":"","asOf":""}]'::jsonb, 'For people in Gurgaon (Gurugram) choosing between many clinics and salons for a hydrafacial, with notes on short sessions around office hours, air-conditioned dryness and heat.', '{}'::jsonb, false, '[]'::jsonb, '["Gurgaon has a dense mix of clinics and mall-based salons that provide hydrafacial sessions.","A lunch-hour session sounds easy, and skin that stays pink for hours is the catch.","Air-conditioned offices dry the skin, so ask what moisturiser fits after a session."]'::jsonb, null, '[{"heading":"Gurgaon or Gurugram","text":"They are the same city. We use Gurgaon here because more people search for it, and the body text also says Gurugram."},{"heading":"Lunch-hour sessions","text":"A session of under an hour fits a lunch break, but pink skin can last a few hours. If you have a meeting, book the last slot of the day instead."},{"heading":"Mall salon or clinic","text":"Both are common here. A clinic can check your skin for sunburn, infection or an irritated barrier. A salon may only follow a fixed menu. Ask who performs the session."},{"heading":"Questions worth writing down","text":"Send the same three questions to each place: who performs it, what is in the base price, and what happens if my skin reacts. Compare the written replies."}]'::jsonb, 'Hydrafacial in Gurgaon: Cost, Downtime, Risks', 'Hydrafacial in Gurgaon', 'A hydrafacial in Gurgaon (also written Gurugram) is a skin-care session of under an hour, with pink skin for a few hours. The local price is {tbc} until quotes are collected. Gurgaon has a dense mix of clinics and mall-based salons, so a quote check matters more than the address.', '[{"heading":"Many choices, one comparison","paragraphs":["Gurgaon has more skin clinics and salons per mile than most cities, and a hydrafacial is on the menu of many. That makes comparison the main task. Look for the same lines in every quote: the base session, each serum, each booster, and the pack total beside the per-session price.","Treat a very low base price with caution until you have seen what it leaves out. Treat pressure to prepay for a pack the same way. Try one session first, and see how your skin reacts."]},{"heading":"Air conditioning, heat and a short session","paragraphs":["Long days in air-conditioned offices can dry the skin, and a hydrafacial exfoliates the surface. Skin may feel tight or sensitive for a day or two. Ask the person who performs your session what moisturiser and sun protection fit your skin.","From April to September the sun and heat are strong. Strong sun on freshly exfoliated skin can irritate it, so cover up and keep outdoor time short for the first day."]},{"heading":"Tap water and the face wash you use","paragraphs":["Groundwater in parts of Gurugram is reported to be hard or salty, and many homes use filters. We do not claim that water changes how a session works. If your skin feels tight after washing at home, mention it, and let the clinic suggest a gentle cleanser."]},{"heading":"Language and asking for a written quote","paragraphs":["Hindi and English are the working languages here. Ask for a written quote that lists each step and add-on. Keep it, because it is the only record of what you agreed to.","If you are unsure about a booster or a serum, ask what it contains and why it is advised for your skin. A specific answer is a good sign, and a vague one is a reason to pause."]},{"heading":"Monsoon and travel","paragraphs":["Heavy rain can cause waterlogging and long delays in July and August. If you plan a session before an event, leave a buffer of days. A rescheduled session costs less than a rushed one on a day when your skin looks irritated."]}]'::jsonb),
  ('hydrafacial', 'delhi', false, false, null, 'Hydrafacial in Delhi: what a session costs, downtime, who should skip it, and how to compare clinic quotes.', null, null, null, null, null, null, null, true, null, null, '{"review":"varies","aftercare":"varies"}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"No partner facility is confirmed in Delhi yet. Hydrafacial sessions are given in dermatology clinics, skin clinics and salons, and the quality of checks differs between them. This page will name the type once one is confirmed. Until then, use the questions below on any place you are considering.","partners":[{"type":"Skin clinic or dermatology clinic in Delhi (to be confirmed)","count":null}],"accreditation":null,"checks":[{"check":"Who performs the session","why":"A doctor, a nurse and a technician have different training","ask":"Who will perform my session, and can I see their training?"},{"check":"Skin check first","why":"Active infection or sunburn means you should wait","ask":"Will someone look at my skin and ask about my medicines before starting?"},{"check":"Tips and tools","why":"Reused tools can spread infection","ask":"Are the tips single-use or cleaned, and how?"},{"check":"Serum and booster list","why":"Add-ons change the bill and can cause reactions","ask":"What is in the base price and what is extra?"},{"check":"Pack pressure","why":"Prepaid packs are hard to refund","ask":"Can I pay for one session first and decide on a pack afterwards?"}]}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"A session is short, so the trip matters more than the treatment. In Delhi a clinic on a metro line or near your office makes it easy to fit a session between work and home.","airport":"Indira Gandhi International Airport (to be verified)","station":"New Delhi, Old Delhi and Hazrat Nizamuddin stations (to be verified against the facility)","stayDays":"Same day. No stay needed","metro":"The metro suits a session visit, and skin may be pink afterwards, so a cap or scarf and sun protection help on the way home. {sample} The nearest station is added once a facility is confirmed.","roadTimes":[{"from":"Noida","time":"50 to 90 min","tip":"A mid-morning slot avoids both peaks"},{"from":"Ghaziabad","time":"60 to 100 min","tip":"Combine the session with another errand in the city"},{"from":"Faridabad","time":"50 to 90 min","tip":"Book the last slot before an evening peak"},{"from":"Gurgaon","time":"50 to 90 min","tip":"Gurgaon has its own clinics, so compare before travelling"}],"privacyNote":"You do not have to tell anyone why you are at the clinic. Ask that messages name the clinic and the time only, and not the session.","mapCaption":"Travel into Delhi from nearby towns, no building shown."}'::jsonb, '[{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: which Delhi facility, if any, will provide hydrafacial sessions","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: winter and post-Diwali air quality in Delhi (public CPCB records, month and station)","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: tap water quality by area of Delhi (public water board reports)","source":"","asOf":""}]'::jsonb, 'For readers in Delhi and the nearby NCR towns who are comparing many clinic and salon quotes for a hydrafacial and want to read them line by line, with notes on winter dryness and wedding dates.', '{}'::jsonb, false, '[]'::jsonb, '["Delhi has many clinics and salons, so comparing quotes line by line is the main task.","Winter dryness and strong summer sun both affect how skin feels after a session.","Book a trial session weeks before a wedding, not days."]'::jsonb, null, '[{"heading":"Clinic or salon","text":"Both give hydrafacial sessions in Delhi. A doctor-led clinic can check your skin and advise against a session. A salon may not. Ask which setting you are in, and who performs the session."},{"heading":"Price comparison","text":"Ask three places for the same lines in writing: the base session, each serum, and any pack. A low base price with many add-ons can end up above a higher base price that includes them."},{"heading":"A weekday slot","text":"Weekday mornings are quieter and let you avoid peak roads. If your skin is pink, you can cover up for the ride home and go back to your routine in the afternoon."},{"heading":"Bring a list of products","text":"Take a list of the creams and acids you use, and anything started in the past few weeks. If you use a retinoid or an acid, say so before the session starts."}]'::jsonb, 'Hydrafacial in Delhi: Cost, Downtime, Risks', 'Hydrafacial in Delhi', 'A hydrafacial in Delhi is a short skin-care session, usually under an hour, with pink skin for a few hours afterwards. The local price is {tbc} until quotes are collected. Delhi has many clinics and salons, so the useful skill is comparing quotes line by line.', '[{"heading":"Reading Delhi quotes line by line","paragraphs":["Delhi has more places that provide a hydrafacial than most cities, and prices vary widely between them. The difference often sits in what is counted. One clinic quotes a base session and adds a serum, a booster and an extra step. Another folds those into one figure.","Write the same questions to each place: what is the base session, which serums are in it, which boosters are extra, what does a pack cost in total and per session, and what happens if my skin reacts. Then compare the totals for the same set of steps."]},{"heading":"Winter dryness and summer sun","paragraphs":["Delhi winters are dry and the air in many weeks is poor, and summers are hot with strong sun. A hydrafacial exfoliates the surface, so skin can feel sensitive to both dryness and sun for a day or two. Ask the clinic what moisturiser and sun protection to use, and how to adjust in each season.","We do not claim that pollution or water changes how a session works. If you notice that your skin reacts more at certain times of year, tell the person who performs it."]},{"heading":"Timing around weddings and events","paragraphs":["Wedding season fills the winter months. A session just before an event is a risk, because redness, a breakout or a reaction would show on the day. Book a trial session at least a few weeks ahead so you know how your skin reacts, and keep a gap before the event.","Avoid trying a new serum, booster or other facial in the last week."]},{"heading":"Language and asking questions","paragraphs":["Staff at most Delhi clinics speak Hindi and English, and many speak Punjabi. If the quote is in English and you read Hindi more easily, ask for a Hindi explanation of each line. Ask who will perform the session and what their training is, and note the answer."]},{"heading":"Where the session sits in a skin routine","paragraphs":["A hydrafacial does not replace a doctor''s plan for acne, pigment or scars. If you are already seeing a dermatologist, tell them you plan a session and ask whether to wait. If you use a retinoid or acid at home, ask whether to pause it before and after."]}]'::jsonb),
