sions and a workday","text":"Ask how long each session takes with preparation and observation, and how much redness to expect. A peel on a Thursday evening leaves a weekend to settle, and a Monday meeting does not."},{"heading":"Compare with Delhi","text":"Many people from South Delhi look at Gurgaon clinics and the reverse. Compare the same plan line by line, and the travel for every visit, not only the price of one session."},{"heading":"Office air","text":"Air-conditioned offices dry the skin. Flaking after a peel feels worse in dry air. Ask the doctor what moisturiser suits your plan."}]'::jsonb, 'Anti-Aging Treatment in Gurgaon: Cost, Downtime, Risks', 'Anti-aging treatment in Gurgaon', 'Anti-aging treatment in Gurgaon (also written Gurugram) means choosing among non-surgical options with a dermatologist. The local sample price per method is {tbc} until quotes are collected. Gurgaon schedules are tight, so the plan has to fit sessions, downtime and work together.', '[{"heading":"Courses and calendars","paragraphs":["Peels, lasers and some devices are given in a course, with weeks between sessions. A course of three to six visits is common for some methods, and the doctor sets the number for you. Put every visit in your calendar before you pay, and check that it fits a month with travel and deadlines.","If a visit falls before an important meeting, move it. Redness, swelling or bruising can last longer than the plan said."]},{"heading":"Long hot summers and cold offices","paragraphs":["Gurgaon summers run from April into September, with strong sun and heat. Treated skin is more sensitive to both, and sun on treated skin can darken marks. Sun protection is the main aftercare question here, and the doctor will say which type fits and how often to reapply.","Cold, dry offices pull moisture from the skin. Ask for a moisturiser plan that works at a desk and outdoors."]},{"heading":"Hard water and facial care","paragraphs":["Groundwater in parts of Gurugram is described as hard or salty, and many homes use filters. We make no claim that this changes the effect of any treatment, and no source is yet attached. If your skin feels tight after washing, tell the doctor, who may suggest a gentler cleanser."]},{"heading":"Referral habits and checking a recommendation","paragraphs":["People in Gurgaon often take a recommendation from a colleague or a friend. A recommendation is a place to start, and not a check. Ask for the doctor''s registration, the written plan and the number of sessions, and compare at least two places.","If a clinic suggests a package of many treatments on the first visit, ask for each part as a separate line, and ask which one part you could start with."]},{"heading":"Monsoon and the schedule","paragraphs":["Heavy rain can cause long delays on the roads in July and August. Leave a buffer for each visit, and ask the clinic how a missed session affects the course. A short delay is rarely a problem, and a gap of many weeks may change the plan."]}]'::jsonb),
  ('anti-aging-treatment', 'delhi', false, false, null, 'Anti-aging treatment in Delhi: sample cost lines per method, downtime, risks, and how to plan sessions and travel from nearby towns.', null, null, null, null, null, null, null, true, null, null, '{"review":"varies","aftercare":"varies"}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"No partner facility is confirmed in Delhi yet. These treatments are given in dermatology clinics, cosmetic clinics and hospital skin departments, and equipment and training differ between them. This page will name the facility type once one is confirmed. Until then, use the questions below.","partners":[{"type":"Dermatology or cosmetic clinic in Delhi (to be confirmed)","count":null}],"accreditation":null,"checks":[{"check":"Registered doctor plans the course","why":"Several of these methods are medical procedures with real risks","ask":"Who assesses me and plans the course, and where can I check the registration?"},{"check":"One option at a time","why":"A plan that adds everything at once makes it hard to tell what helped","ask":"Can the plan start with one method and add another after a review?"},{"check":"Written plan with sessions and total","why":"Packages hide the cost per session","ask":"Can I have each method, the sessions and the total in writing?"},{"check":"Who performs each treatment","why":"Training differs between a doctor, a nurse and a technician","ask":"Who performs each treatment, and what is their training? In a large city, ask for the answer in writing."},{"check":"Plan for a problem","why":"A burn, a lump or a reaction needs a plan and a number to call","ask":"What do I do if I have blistering, a lump or severe pain, and who do I call?"}]}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"A plan with several sessions means several trips. In Delhi, a clinic on a metro line near your work makes a course of visits easier to keep.","airport":"Indira Gandhi International Airport (to be verified)","station":"New Delhi, Old Delhi and Hazrat Nizamuddin stations (to be verified against the facility)","stayDays":"Same day. No stay for consultations and sessions","metro":"The metro suits a session visit. After a peel or laser, skin can be red and sensitive to sun, so a cab with the window up or a cover-up helps. {sample} The nearest station is added once a facility is confirmed.","roadTimes":[{"from":"Noida","time":"50 to 90 min","tip":"Ask for the same weekday and time for every session"},{"from":"Ghaziabad","time":"60 to 100 min","tip":"Ask which reviews can be a video call with photos"},{"from":"Faridabad","time":"50 to 90 min","tip":"Book the next session before you leave"},{"from":"Gurgaon","time":"50 to 90 min","tip":"Gurgaon has its own clinics, so compare before you travel"}],"privacyNote":"You do not have to explain a visit to anyone. Skin photos are health data, so ask where clinic photos are stored. Ask that messages name the clinic and time only.","mapCaption":"Travel into Delhi from nearby towns, no building shown."}'::jsonb, '[{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: which Delhi facility, if any, will provide these treatments, and its type","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: winter and post-Diwali air quality in Delhi (public CPCB records, month and station)","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: seasonal sun and heat for Delhi (IMD climate normals)","source":"","asOf":""}]'::jsonb, 'For readers in Delhi and the nearby NCR towns who are comparing many anti-aging options and clinics, with notes on pigmentation questions, winter dryness against summer sun and wedding-season timing.', '{}'::jsonb, false, '[]'::jsonb, '["Delhi has so many methods that the first job is to choose one concern and one method.","Pollution and pigmentation questions belong with a dermatologist, and we make no claim about them.","Winter dryness and summer sun point to different months for peels and lasers."]'::jsonb, null, '[{"heading":"Start with one concern","text":"Pick the feature that bothers you most, for example lines between the brows or uneven tone, and ask the doctor which one method suits it. Adding several at once makes it hard to judge any of them."},{"heading":"Pigmentation questions","text":"People in Delhi often ask whether air quality affects dark marks and tone. We make no claim here. Ask the dermatologist what is known and what it means for the plan you are considering. {pending}"},{"heading":"Winter or summer","text":"Peels and lasers leave skin red and sensitive to sun. Many doctors prefer to plan them away from the strongest sun. Ask what suits your skin and the month you want to start."},{"heading":"Packages","text":"A package of several treatments is easy to buy and hard to compare. Ask for each method, its number of sessions and its price on separate lines before you pay."}]'::jsonb, 'Anti-Aging Treatment in Delhi: Cost, Downtime, Risks', 'Anti-aging treatment in Delhi', 'Anti-aging treatment in Delhi means a choice among non-surgical options, planned by a dermatologist after looking at your skin. The local sample price per method is {tbc} until quotes are collected. Delhi has many clinics and many methods, so the useful step is to start with one concern and one method.', '[{"heading":"Too many choices in a big city","paragraphs":["Delhi has more clinics and more methods than most cities, and a visit to a few can end with five suggestions. That is a reason to slow down. Ask each doctor which single concern is most suitable to treat, which method addresses it, and how you will tell whether it worked.","A good plan has a first step, a review date and a point at which you stop or change. If a plan does not, ask for them in writing."]},{"heading":"Dry winters and strong summer sun","paragraphs":["Delhi winters are dry and summers are hot with strong sun. Peels, lasers and some devices leave skin red and more sensitive to sun for days, and sun on treated skin can darken marks. The doctor may prefer to plan these away from the strongest sun and to put sun protection first.","Dry months can make flaking more uncomfortable. Ask what moisturiser fits your plan and how to adjust it in each season."]},{"heading":"Weddings and the last month before an event","paragraphs":["Wedding season fills the winter months in Delhi. Start any plan several weeks before a date, so that downtime and an adjustment are done in time. Do not add a new treatment, a new cream or a stronger peel in the last week.","If you are a guest and not the bride or groom, the same applies. A trial session with time to settle is better than a rush."]},{"heading":"Language, referral and second opinions","paragraphs":["Staff at most Delhi clinics speak Hindi and English, and some speak Punjabi. Ask for the written plan in the language you read most easily. A second opinion from a dermatologist you trust is reasonable before a large plan, and a plan that is good will stand up to it."]},{"heading":"Water and your daily routine","paragraphs":["Tap water in parts of Delhi is described as hard. We make no claim that it changes the effect of any treatment. If your skin feels tight after washing, tell the doctor, who can suggest a gentler cleanser. Keep the routine simple before and after any session."]}]'::jsonb),
