(to be verified against the facility)","stayDays":"Same day for most visits. No stay for consultations and sessions","metro":"The Lucknow Metro runs along a north-south line and suits a consultation in the city. After a peel or laser, a cab with the window up keeps sun and dust off the skin. {sample} Stations near a facility are added once it is confirmed.","roadTimes":[{"from":"Barabanki","time":"40 to 70 min","tip":"Short enough for a session and a same-day return"},{"from":"Unnao","time":"60 to 100 min","tip":"Book the earliest slot to avoid afternoon heat"},{"from":"Sitapur","time":"80 to 120 min","tip":"Ask whether reviews can be by video"},{"from":"Hardoi","time":"100 to 150 min","tip":"Plan sessions on days you are in the city anyway"}],"privacyNote":"In a smaller town a neighbour may recognise you at a clinic. A quiet slot or a different waiting area can help, and the clinic should keep the treatment name out of messages.","mapCaption":"Travel into Lucknow from nearby districts, no building shown."}'::jsonb, '[{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: which Lucknow facility, if any, will provide these treatments, and its type","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: Lucknow climate normals for heat, humidity and fog (IMD)","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: road times from Barabanki, Unnao, Sitapur and Hardoi, checked on a map with a date","source":"","asOf":""}]'::jsonb, 'For readers in Lucknow and nearby districts who need to plan repeat trips for a multi-session course, with notes on May and June heat for peels and lasers, wedding season and a link to Kanpur.', '{}'::jsonb, false, '[]'::jsonb, '["A course of peels or laser sessions from Unnao means a series of trips.","May and June sun and heat suit peels and lasers poorly, so ask about timing.","Lucknow fills with events in the wedding season, and clinics and roads fill with it."]'::jsonb, null, '[{"heading":"Count the trips first","text":"Ask the doctor how many sessions and reviews the plan needs, and count each one as a day trip. A plan of six visits from Sitapur is a different commitment from the same plan from Gomti Nagar."},{"heading":"Areas people ask about","text":"People often ask about clinics in Gomti Nagar, Hazratganj and Indira Nagar. We name no clinic. Choose by the doctor, the plan in writing and the number of trips, and then by distance."},{"heading":"Summer sun and dust","text":"May and June are hot and dusty, and treated skin is more sensitive to both. Ask whether to schedule peels and lasers in cooler months, and which sun protection fits your skin."},{"heading":"Compare with Kanpur","text":"If you live between the two cities, compare the road time to each and the plan in each. Kanpur is the nearest other city we cover."}]'::jsonb, 'Anti-Aging Treatment in Lucknow: Cost, Downtime, Risks', 'Anti-aging treatment in Lucknow', 'Anti-aging treatment in Lucknow means choosing among non-surgical options with a dermatologist. The local sample price per method is {tbc} until quotes are collected. Many people travel in from nearby towns, so the number of trips a plan needs is as important as its price.', '[{"heading":"Plan the course, not one session","paragraphs":["A single treatment rarely stands alone. Peels, lasers and tightening devices come in courses, and injections are repeated as the effect fades. Ask for the whole plan, with the number of sessions, the gaps between them and the total. From a nearby town, a series of day trips is the real cost to count.","Ask whether a review can be a video call with photos taken in daylight, and which problems need you in person. Write down where to go for urgent care near home."]},{"heading":"Heat, dust and the strongest sun","paragraphs":["Lucknow summers are hot and dry, with the strongest sun in May and June. The monsoon is humid, and winter mornings can be foggy. Sun on treated skin can darken marks, so many doctors prefer to plan peels and lasers for cooler months. The reviewer will confirm what applies.","On any day after a session, carry a cap or an umbrella and use the sun protection the doctor names."]},{"heading":"Water and the daily routine","paragraphs":["Households use a mix of piped supply and groundwater, and hardness varies by area. We make no claim that water changes the effect of any treatment. If your skin feels tight after washing, tell the doctor, and ask for a gentler cleanser."]},{"heading":"Weddings, festivals and timing","paragraphs":["Wedding season, Diwali and Eid make roads and clinics busy. Start any plan several weeks before a date, and avoid new treatments in the last week. If a family wedding is the reason, book the first session soon, because a course takes weeks to run."]},{"heading":"Hindi, referrals and being told the truth","paragraphs":["The consultation can be in Hindi or Hinglish. Ask the doctor to explain each option, including what it cannot do, and to write the plan in a language you read easily. {tbc}","In smaller towns people often hear of a clinic from a relative. Ask your local doctor whether the plan makes sense, and compare it with a second plan before you pay for a package."]}]'::jsonb),
  ('anti-aging-treatment', 'kanpur', false, false, null, 'Anti-aging treatment in Kanpur: sample cost lines per method, downtime, risks, and how to plan 3 to 6 visits including trips to Lucknow.', null, null, null, null, null, null, null, true, null, null, '{"review":"varies","aftercare":"varies"}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"No partner facility is confirmed in Kanpur, and Lucknow is the nearest other city we cover. If treatment is in Lucknow, we will say so at the top of this page, with the trip time. Until then, this page shows how to plan a course of visits and what to check.","partners":[{"type":"Dermatology or cosmetic clinic in Kanpur (to be confirmed)","count":null}],"accreditation":null,"checks":[{"check":"Registered doctor plans the course","why":"Several of these methods are medical procedures with real risks","ask":"Who assesses me and plans the course, and where can I check the registration?"},{"check":"One option at a time","why":"A plan that adds everything at once makes it hard to tell what helped","ask":"Can the plan start with one method and add another after a review?"},{"check":"Written plan with sessions and total","why":"Packages hide the cost per session","ask":"Can I have each method, the sessions and the total in writing?"},{"check":"Who performs each treatment","why":"Training differs between a doctor, a nurse and a technician","ask":"Who performs each treatment, and what is their training? If care is in Lucknow, ask which visits must be there."},{"check":"Plan for a problem","why":"A burn, a lump or a reaction needs a plan and a number to call","ask":"What do I do if I have blistering, a lump or severe pain, and who do I call?"}]}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"A plan with several visits is a plan for repeat trips. Settle which visits are in Kanpur and which, if any, are in Lucknow before you start.","airport":"Kanpur civil airport and Lucknow airport (service and schedules to be verified)","station":"Kanpur Central, and Charbagh in Lucknow (to be verified)","stayDays":"Same day for Kanpur visits. A Lucknow visit is a day trip","metro":"Kanpur has a metro line that is partly open, and the part open is to be checked against any facility. {sample} After a peel or laser, a cab is easier on the skin than a crowded vehicle.","roadTimes":[{"from":"Unnao","time":"30 to 60 min","tip":"Close enough for a session and a same-day return"},{"from":"Kanpur Dehat","time":"40 to 80 min","tip":"An early slot avoids afternoon heat"},{"from":"Fatehpur","time":"70 to 110 min","tip":"Ask for longer gaps between sessions if the doctor agrees"},{"from":"Lucknow","time":"100 to 150 min","tip":"The other city we cover. Compare the trips before you commit"}],"privacyNote":"In a mid-sized city many people know each other. You do not have to explain the visit, and a clinic should keep the treatment name out of messages.","mapCaption":"Travel into Kanpur from nearby towns, and the road to Lucknow, no building shown."}'::jsonb, '[{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: whether any partner facility exists in Kanpur for these treatments, and its type","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: Kanpur road time and train timings to Lucknow, from a map with a date","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: Kanpur air quality record (public CPCB station data)","source":"","asOf":""}]'::jsonb, 'For readers in Kanpur and nearby towns who need to plan three to six visits, decide which stay local and which are in Lucknow, and ask about dust and industrial air without a claim being made for them.', '{}'::jsonb, false, '[]'::jsonb, '["In Kanpur a plan of three to six visits needs a decision on what stays local and what goes to Lucknow.","Dust and industrial air are common questions, and no claim is made without a source.","A link to Lucknow shows the road time and the plan in the nearest other city we cover."]'::jsonb, null, '[{"heading":"Three to six visits","text":"Many multi-session plans need three to six visits. Write each one on a calendar with the date, the place and the purpose, and add the travel. If the total is more than you can manage, tell the doctor, who can plan around it."},{"heading":"Dust and industrial air","text":"Kanpur is an industrial city, and people ask whether dust affects skin after treatments. We make no claim here. Ask the dermatologist how to protect and clean treated skin. {pending}"},{"heading":"Compare with Lucknow","text":"If the plan is in Lucknow, compare the road or train time and the cost of each trip with a plan in Kanpur. The nearest other city we cover is Lucknow."},{"heading":"Cold winters and hot summers","text":"Winters are cold and dry, and summers are hot with strong sun. Both matter for treated skin. Ask the doctor which months suit peels and lasers for your skin."}]'::jsonb, 'Anti-Aging Treatment in Kanpur: Cost, Downtime, Risks', 'Anti-aging treatment in Kanpur', 'Anti-aging treatment in Kanpur means choosing among non-surgical options with a dermatologist, and many plans need three to six visits. The local sample price per method is {tbc} until quotes are collected. No partner facility is confirmed in Kanpur yet, so how to plan repeat trips, and whether some go to Lucknow, comes first.', '[{"heading":"Planning three to six visits","paragraphs":["Peels, lasers, skin boosters and tightening devices come in courses, and a course can mean three to six visits. For someone in Kanpur, each visit is a trip. Start by writing the whole plan on a calendar, with the date, the place and the purpose of each visit. If a plan has more visits than you can attend, tell the doctor before you pay.","Ask which visits are procedures and which are checks. Checks can sometimes be done by video or by a local doctor, if the plan is written down."]},{"heading":"What can stay in Kanpur","paragraphs":["A local doctor can often see you for a simple check, such as irritated skin or a question about a cream. They cannot usually do what the dermatologist who made the plan does. Ask the planning doctor which changes a local doctor may make, and write the doctor''s name on your plan."]},{"heading":"Dust, heat and cold","paragraphs":["Kanpur has cold dry winters and hot summers. Cold air dries skin and makes flaking after a peel more noticeable. Heat and dust call for gentle cleansing and sun cover. We make no claim that dust or industrial air changes the effect of any treatment.","Ask what to wear outdoors after a peel or laser, and how often to clean your face. Do not add scrubs or home remedies."]},{"heading":"Water and the daily routine","paragraphs":["Water supply in the city mixes the river, piped supply and groundwater, and hardness differs by neighbourhood. We make no claim that water changes the effect of any treatment. If skin feels tight after washing, tell the doctor, and ask for a gentler cleanser."]},{"heading":"Referral, language and winter travel","paragraphs":["Hindi and Hinglish are common in clinics. Ask for the plan in the language you read most easily. A family doctor can refer you and keep your notes, which helps if you see two doctors in two cities.","Winter fog can slow roads and trains to Lucknow. Book the earliest slot, allow spare time and avoid a long ride straight after a peel or laser, when skin is red and sensitive."]}]'::jsonb),
  ('prp-treatment', 'gurgaon', false, false, null, 'PRP treatment in Gurgaon (Gurugram): sample cost lines, sessions, recovery, risks and how to reach the clinic from Delhi. Results vary.', null, null, null, null, null, null, null, true, null, null, '{"review":"varies","aftercare":"varies"}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"A partner facility exists in Gurgaon for other treatments, and whether it provides PRP is to be confirmed. We do not name it. In this city PRP is given in day-care clinics and dermatology clinics, so ask what kind of place you are in.","partners":[{"type":"Day-care facility or clinic in Gurgaon (to be confirmed)","count":null}],"accreditation":null,"checks":[{"check":"Registered doctor","why":"PRP involves a needle and a blood draw, and a doctor should plan it","ask":"Who examines me and plans the course, and where can I check the registration?"},{"check":"Single-use sealed kit","why":"Reused kits can spread infection","ask":"Is the kit single-use and sealed, and will I see it opened?"},{"check":"Sessions and total in writing","why":"A course is the real price, and one session is not","ask":"Can I have the number of sessions, the gap and the total in writing?"},{"check":"What if there is no change","why":"Evidence is mixed, so a plan for no change matters","ask":"What is the plan if I see no change after the course? Ask whether the same doctor sees you at every session."},{"check":"Medical causes checked","why":"Hair thinning can have a medical cause that needs its own care","ask":"Will you check for thyroid, iron or hormone causes before starting?"}]}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"Most people fit a PRP course around the working week. Choose a clinic near your office or on your commute, and ask which evening slots are kept for repeat sessions.","airport":"Indira Gandhi International Airport, Delhi (to be verified)","station":"HUDA City Centre (Yellow Line) and Sikandarpur (Rapid Metro)","stayDays":"Same day. No stay for sessions","metro":"Sikandarpur and HUDA City Centre serve much of the commercial belt. After a scalp session, a cap and a short cab are easier than a long walk in the heat. {sample} The distance to a facility is added once one is confirmed.","roadTimes":[{"from":"South Delhi","time":"40 to 70 min","tip":"An evening slot may cross the highway rush, so try mid-morning"},{"from":"Noida","time":"70 to 110 min","tip":"Check clinics in Noida before you commit to a course here"},{"from":"Faridabad","time":"60 to 100 min","tip":"A weekend slot suits a course spaced by weeks"},{"from":"Rewari","time":"60 to 90 min","tip":"Plan sessions on days you are in the city anyway"}],"privacyNote":"Many clients come from nearby offices. You do not need to explain visits to colleagues. Ask the clinic to keep the treatment name out of messages and reminders.","mapCaption":"Travel into Gurgaon from Delhi and nearby towns, no building shown."}'::jsonb, '[{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: whether the Gurgaon partner facility provides PRP, and its type","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: groundwater hardness for Gurugram (Central Ground Water Board report, year)","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: Rapid Metro and road route to the facility, with a date","source":"","asOf":""}]'::jsonb, 'For people in Gurgaon (Gurugram) who plan a PRP course around office hours, with notes on evening slots, the Rapid Metro, the naming of the city, hard-water questions with no claim attached, and coming from Delhi each time.', '{}'::jsonb, false, '[]'::jsonb, '["In Gurgaon a PRP course has to fit an office week, so evening slots and the Rapid Metro come first.","The question of coming from Delhi each time is about the number of trips and not only about distance.","Hard water is a common question here, and no claim is made without a source."]'::jsonb, null, '[{"heading":"Gurgaon or Gurugram","text":"They are the same city. We use Gurgaon here because more people search for it, and the body text also says Gurugram. Either spelling works when you ask a clinic."},{"heading":"Evening slots after office","text":"Some clinics keep evening slots. Ask which days and until what time. An evening scalp session lets you go home and rest, and you avoid an office meeting with a red or tender scalp."},{"heading":"The Rapid Metro route","text":"Sikandarpur is on the Rapid Metro and HUDA City Centre is on the Yellow Line. Ask the clinic how far it is from either, and check the walk or the cab you will need on a hot day."},{"heading":"Coming from Delhi each time","text":"People travel from South Delhi and nearby towns. Compare Delhi and Gurgaon plans on the number of trips and the total, and not only on the price of one session. Delhi is the nearest other city we cover."}]'::jsonb, 'PRP Treatment in Gurgaon: Cost, Sessions, Risks', 'PRP treatment in Gurgaon', 'PRP treatment in Gurgaon (also written Gurugram) is a course of short visits, usually fitted around office hours. The local sample cost per session is {tbc} until quotes are collected. Evidence is mixed and results vary, so ask what the plan is if you see no change.', '[{"heading":"A course around an office week","paragraphs":["PRP is not a one-visit treatment. A course of several sessions, spaced by weeks, competes with deadlines, travel and holidays in a Gurgaon work year. Before you pay for a course, put each session on a calendar and check the weeks around it.","Ask whether the first and second sessions are close together or spaced, and how many weeks the plan allows to pass before a review. If the plan has a long gap in the middle, ask why."]},{"heading":"Heat, air conditioning and scalp care","paragraphs":["Gurgaon summers run from April into September, with heat and sweat. After a scalp session, the doctor will say when to wash your hair and when to avoid heat and hard exercise. Air-conditioned offices dry the skin, so skin PRP aftercare may need a moisturiser, and the doctor will say which kind.","We make no claim that heat or air conditioning changes how PRP works."]},{"heading":"Hard water, shampoo and hair questions","paragraphs":["Groundwater in parts of Gurugram is described as hard or salty, and many people ask whether it affects their hair. We make no claim that water causes hair thinning, and no source is yet attached. Ask the doctor which shampoo suits your scalp and how often to wash."]},{"heading":"Referral habits and asking a second doctor","paragraphs":["People often take a clinic name from a colleague. A name is a place to start, and not a check. Ask for the registration, the written plan, the number of sessions and what the plan is if you see no change. A second opinion from a dermatologist you already see is a good step.","Be careful of a package of many sessions on the first day, and ask for the price of one session by itself."]},{"heading":"Monsoon and keeping the rhythm","paragraphs":["Heavy rain can cause long delays in July and August. Leave a buffer for each visit. A session delayed by a week or two is usually acceptable, and the clinic can tell you how much delay the plan allows."]}]'::jsonb),
  ('prp-treatment', 'delhi', false, false, null, 'PRP treatment in Delhi: sample cost lines, sessions, recovery, risks and how to reach the clinic from Noida, Ghaziabad or Faridabad. Results vary.', null, null, null, null, null, null, null, true, null, null, '{"review":"varies","aftercare":"varies"}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"No partner facility is confirmed in Delhi yet. PRP is given in day-care clinics and dermatology clinics, not hospital wards. This page will name the facility type once one is confirmed. Until then, use the questions below on any place you are considering.","partners":[{"type":"Day-care facility or clinic in Delhi (to be confirmed)","count":null}],"accreditation":null,"checks":[{"check":"Registered doctor","why":"PRP involves a needle and a blood draw, and a doctor should plan it","ask":"Who examines me and plans the course, and where can I check the registration?"},{"check":"Single-use sealed kit","why":"Reused kits can spread infection","ask":"Is the kit single-use and sealed, and will I see it opened?"},{"check":"Sessions and total in writing","why":"A course is the real price, and one session is not","ask":"Can I have the number of sessions, the gap and the total in writing?"},{"check":"What if there is no change","why":"Evidence is mixed, so a plan for no change matters","ask":"What is the plan if I see no change after the course? Ask for the answer in writing."},{"check":"Medical causes checked","why":"Hair thinning can have a medical cause that needs its own care","ask":"Will you check for thyroid, iron or hormone causes before starting?"}]}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"A PRP course repeats a short visit every few weeks, so it suits a clinic close to work or on your metro line. Delhi traffic decides how long each visit really takes.","airport":"Indira Gandhi International Airport (to be verified)","station":"New Delhi, Old Delhi and Hazrat Nizamuddin stations (to be verified against the facility)","stayDays":"Same day. No stay for sessions","metro":"The metro suits a session on a workday. Go home rather than to the gym, and cover up on the way if skin or scalp is red. {sample} The nearest station is added once a facility is confirmed.","roadTimes":[{"from":"Noida","time":"50 to 90 min","tip":"Fix the same weekday and slot for every session"},{"from":"Ghaziabad","time":"60 to 100 min","tip":"Ask which reviews can be a video call with photos"},{"from":"Faridabad","time":"50 to 90 min","tip":"Book the next session before you leave"},{"from":"Gurgaon","time":"50 to 90 min","tip":"Gurgaon has its own clinics, so compare before you commit to a course"}],"privacyNote":"You do not have to explain visits to anyone. Photos of your scalp or skin are health data, so ask where clinic photos are stored and who can see them.","mapCaption":"Travel into Delhi from nearby towns, no building shown."}'::jsonb, '[{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: which Delhi facility, if any, will provide PRP, and its type","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: winter and post-Diwali air quality in Delhi (public CPCB records, month and station)","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: tap water hardness by area of Delhi (public water board reports)","source":"","asOf":""}]'::jsonb, 'For readers in Delhi and the nearby NCR towns who need to fit a course of PRP visits around work, with notes on metro and traffic planning, winter air and dryness, and hard-water questions that carry no claim.', '{}'::jsonb, false, '[]'::jsonb, '["A PRP course in Delhi is a series of short visits, so a clinic on your metro line matters.","People ask about winter air and hair or skin, and we make no claim about it.","Fix the same weekday and slot for every session, so the course keeps its rhythm."]'::jsonb, null, '[{"heading":"Work-day sessions","text":"A session is short. Many people book it near the office, and go home afterwards. If your scalp is red or tender, a cap and a quiet afternoon are easier than a meeting."},{"heading":"Spacing and your calendar","text":"Sessions are spaced weeks apart. Put every date in your calendar when you book the course, and check it against travel, festivals and exams. A long gap in the middle of a course changes the plan."},{"heading":"Winter air and skin PRP","text":"People ask whether Delhi''s winter air changes the timing of PRP for the face. We make no claim here. Ask the dermatologist what is known and how to protect treated skin. {pending}"},{"heading":"Hard water and your scalp","text":"Tap water in parts of Delhi is described as hard, and people ask about hair. We make no claim that water causes hair thinning. Ask the doctor which shampoo and how often to wash after a session."}]'::jsonb, 'PRP Treatment in Delhi: Cost, Sessions, Risks', 'PRP treatment in Delhi', 'PRP treatment in Delhi is usually a course of short visits, so travel time counts as much as the price of one session. The local sample cost per session is {tbc} until quotes are collected. Evidence for PRP is mixed and results vary, so ask what the plan is if you see no change.', '[{"heading":"A course in a city of long distances","paragraphs":["A PRP course is several short visits across weeks or months. In Delhi the length of each visit is the road. Choose a clinic on a metro line or near your workplace, and ask for the same slot every time, so that it becomes a habit rather than a planning problem.","Count the trips before you pay. A plan with six sessions and two reviews is eight trips. If the number is more than you can keep, tell the doctor, who may plan a shorter course or longer gaps."]},{"heading":"Winter dryness, pollution questions and summer sweat","paragraphs":["Delhi winters are dry and the air in many weeks is poor, and summers are hot and sweaty. After a scalp session, the doctor will say when you can wash your hair and what to use. After a face session, sun protection matters. We make no claim that pollution or heat changes how PRP works.","If you sweat a lot, ask how to manage the first day or two, because the advice may be to avoid heavy exercise and heat."]},{"heading":"Referral and the question of medical causes","paragraphs":["Many people in Delhi come to PRP after seeing a family doctor or after trying a shampoo or a supplement. If hair thinning is the reason, ask whether your thyroid, iron and hormone levels have been checked. Bring any reports.","A second opinion is reasonable before a course. A plan that is good will stand up to it."]},{"heading":"Language and written answers","paragraphs":["Staff at most Delhi clinics speak Hindi and English, and some speak Punjabi. Ask for the course plan in the language you read most easily. Ask the doctor what counts as a change and what the plan is if there is none. {tbc}"]},{"heading":"Wedding season and event timing","paragraphs":["A scalp or face session does not look like much, but marks and swelling can show for days. If you have a wedding or event, plan sessions weeks ahead and avoid a session in the final days."]}]'::jsonb),
  ('prp-treatment', 'lucknow', false, false, null, 'PRP treatment in Lucknow: sample cost lines, sessions, recovery, risks and how to reach the clinic from Barabanki, Unnao and Sitapur. Results vary.', null, null, null, null, null, null, null, true, null, null, '{"review":"varies","aftercare":"varies"}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"No partner facility is confirmed in Lucknow yet. PRP is given in day-care clinics and dermatology clinics. If care ends up in another city, we will say so at the top of this page and not claim a local site.","partners":[{"type":"Day-care facility or clinic in Lucknow (to be confirmed)","count":null}],"accreditation":null,"checks":[{"check":"Registered doctor","why":"PRP involves a needle and a blood draw, and a doctor should plan it","ask":"Who examines me and plans the course, and where can I check the registration?"},{"check":"Single-use sealed kit","why":"Reused kits can spread infection","ask":"Is the kit single-use and sealed, and will I see it opened?"},{"check":"Sessions and total in writing","why":"A course is the real price, and one session is not","ask":"Can I have the number of sessions, the gap and the total in writing?"},{"check":"What if there is no change","why":"Evidence is mixed, so a plan for no change matters","ask":"What is the plan if I see no change after the course? From a nearby town, ask who sees you if something goes wrong between sessions."},{"check":"Medical causes checked","why":"Hair thinning can have a medical cause that needs its own care","ask":"Will you check for thyroid, iron or hormone causes before starting?"}]}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"A PRP course repeats a short visit every few weeks. From a district town, that is a series of day trips, so plan them as a set and not one at a time.","airport":"Chaudhary Charan Singh International Airport, Lucknow (to be verified)","station":"Charbagh station and the Lucknow Metro (to be verified against the facility)","stayDays":"Same day. No stay for sessions","metro":"The Lucknow Metro runs along a north-south line and suits a consultation in the city. After a scalp session, a cab with a cap keeps sun and dust off a tender scalp. {sample} Stations near a facility are added once it is confirmed.","roadTimes":[{"from":"Barabanki","time":"40 to 70 min","tip":"Short enough for a session and a same-day return"},{"from":"Unnao","time":"60 to 100 min","tip":"Book the earliest slot to avoid afternoon heat"},{"from":"Sitapur","time":"80 to 120 min","tip":"Ask whether reviews can be by video"},{"from":"Hardoi","time":"100 to 150 min","tip":"Plan sessions on days you are in the city anyway"}],"privacyNote":"In a smaller town a neighbour may recognise you at a clinic. A quiet slot or a different waiting area can help, and the clinic should keep the treatment name out of messages.","mapCaption":"Travel into Lucknow from nearby districts, no building shown."}'::jsonb, '[{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: which Lucknow facility, if any, will provide PRP, and its type","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: road times from Barabanki, Unnao, Sitapur and Hardoi, checked on a map with a date","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: Lucknow climate normals for heat, dust and humidity (IMD) and Gomti water supply hardness","source":"","asOf":""}]'::jsonb, 'For readers in Lucknow and nearby districts who must plan a PRP course as a series of day trips, with notes on spacing sessions around holidays, a Hindi-speaking coordinator, summer sweat and dust on a tender scalp.', '{}'::jsonb, false, '[]'::jsonb, '["From a district town, a PRP course is a series of day trips that are planned as a set.","Sessions can be spaced around festivals and holidays if the doctor agrees.","A Hindi-speaking coordinator helps with the plan and with the aftercare."]'::jsonb, null, '[{"heading":"Do I travel for every session","text":"Ask which visits need you in person and which can be a video call with photos. A session needs you at the clinic, and a review often does not. Count only the sessions as trips, and plan the rest."},{"heading":"Spacing around holidays","text":"Sessions are spaced weeks apart, so you can choose dates that fit festivals, Eid and holidays, if the doctor agrees. Fix the dates for the whole course at the first visit."},{"heading":"Hindi-speaking coordinator","text":"The consultation and the first calls can be in Hindi or Hinglish. Ask for a coordinator who speaks Hindi, and for the plan and the aftercare written in the language you read most easily. {tbc}"},{"heading":"Areas people ask about","text":"People often ask about clinics in Gomti Nagar, Hazratganj and Indira Nagar. We name no clinic. Choose by the doctor and the written plan, and then by distance and the trips you need to make."}]'::jsonb, 'PRP Treatment in Lucknow: Cost, Sessions, Risks', 'PRP treatment in Lucknow', 'PRP treatment in Lucknow is a course of short visits, and many people travel in from nearby towns for each one. The local sample cost per session is {tbc} until quotes are collected. Evidence is mixed and results vary, so count the trips and ask what the plan is if you see no change.', '[{"heading":"A course as a set of day trips","paragraphs":["PRP is a course of several short sessions. For someone from Unnao or Sitapur, each session is a trip that takes most of a day. Before you pay, write the whole course on a calendar with the dates, and check it against work, farming seasons, exams and festivals.","If the total of trips is more than you can manage, say so at the consultation. A doctor may plan a shorter course or longer gaps, or tell you plainly that PRP is not a good fit."]},{"heading":"Dust, summer sweat and the scalp","paragraphs":["Lucknow summers are hot and dry, with dust, and the monsoon is humid. After a scalp session the doctor will say when you can wash your hair and what to avoid, and the advice for a hot, sweaty day may differ from a cool one. Ask what to do on the first day in May or June.","We make no claim that dust or humidity changes how PRP works. If your scalp is sore or you see pus, call the clinic."]},{"heading":"Water and hair washing","paragraphs":["Households use a mix of piped supply and groundwater, and hardness varies by area. People ask whether water affects hair. We make no claim that it causes hair thinning. Ask the doctor which shampoo suits your scalp and how often to wash."]},{"heading":"Referrals from a local doctor","paragraphs":["In smaller towns, many people hear about PRP from a local doctor, a pharmacist or a relative. Ask the local doctor whether it suits you, and whether your thyroid, iron and hormone levels have been checked. Bring any reports.","Be careful of a phone call or a message that quotes a price before a doctor has seen you. A registered doctor should examine you first."]},{"heading":"Seasons, festivals and fog","paragraphs":["Wedding season, Diwali and Eid fill roads and clinics. Winter fog can delay roads and trains. Plan the course so that no session falls on a day when travel is likely to be hard, and keep a spare date in the calendar."]}]'::jsonb),
  ('prp-treatment', 'kanpur', false, false, null, 'PRP treatment in Kanpur: sample cost lines, sessions, recovery, risks and how to reach the clinic from Unnao and Kanpur Dehat. Results vary.', null, null, null, null, null, null, null, true, null, null, '{"review":"varies","aftercare":"varies"}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"No partner facility is confirmed in Kanpur, and Lucknow is the nearest other city we cover. If PRP is given in Lucknow, we will say so at the top of this page, with the trip time. Until then, this page shows how to plan a course and what to check.","partners":[{"type":"Day-care facility or clinic in Kanpur (to be confirmed)","count":null}],"accreditation":null,"checks":[{"check":"Registered doctor","why":"PRP involves a needle and a blood draw, and a doctor should plan it","ask":"Who examines me and plans the course, and where can I check the registration?"},{"check":"Single-use sealed kit","why":"Reused kits can spread infection","ask":"Is the kit single-use and sealed, and will I see it opened?"},{"check":"Sessions and total in writing","why":"A course is the real price, and one session is not","ask":"Can I have the number of sessions, the gap and the total in writing?"},{"check":"What if there is no change","why":"Evidence is mixed, so a plan for no change matters","ask":"What is the plan if I see no change after the course? If care is in Lucknow, ask which visits must be there."},{"check":"Medical causes checked","why":"Hair thinning can have a medical cause that needs its own care","ask":"Will you check for thyroid, iron or hormone causes before starting?"}]}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"A PRP course repeats a short visit every four to six weeks in many plans. For Kanpur, plan the interval around a trip you can make again and again.","airport":"Kanpur civil airport and Lucknow airport (service and schedules to be verified)","station":"Kanpur Central, and Charbagh in Lucknow (to be verified)","stayDays":"Same day for Kanpur visits. A Lucknow visit is a day trip","metro":"Kanpur has a metro line that is partly open, and the part open is to be checked against any facility. {sample} After a scalp session, a cab with a cap is easier than a crowded vehicle.","roadTimes":[{"from":"Unnao","time":"30 to 60 min","tip":"Close enough for a session and a same-day return"},{"from":"Kanpur Dehat","time":"40 to 80 min","tip":"An early slot avoids afternoon heat"},{"from":"Fatehpur","time":"70 to 110 min","tip":"Ask whether the gap between sessions can be longer"},{"from":"Lucknow","time":"100 to 150 min","tip":"The other city we cover. Compare the trips before you commit to a course"}],"privacyNote":"In a mid-sized city many people know each other. You do not have to explain visits, and a clinic should keep the treatment name out of messages.","mapCaption":"Travel into Kanpur from nearby towns, and the road to Lucknow, no building shown."}'::jsonb, '[{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: whether any partner facility exists in Kanpur for PRP, and its type","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: Kanpur to Lucknow rail timings and road time, from a map or timetable with a date","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: Kanpur air quality record (public CPCB station data) and groundwater hardness","source":"","asOf":""}]'::jsonb, 'For readers in Kanpur and nearby towns who must decide whether PRP sessions are local or in Lucknow, with notes on train timings for a four to six week interval, local reviews, and dust and hard-water questions that carry no claim.', '{}'::jsonb, false, '[]'::jsonb, '["In Kanpur a PRP course raises one question first: do sessions happen here or in Lucknow.","A four to six week gap suits a regular train or road trip if the timings are checked.","Reviews may be done locally if the plan is written down for a Kanpur doctor."]'::jsonb, null, '[{"heading":"Do I travel to Lucknow","text":"If PRP is given only in Lucknow, each session is a day trip. Ask whether any part of the course can be in Kanpur, and which visits need the doctor who made the plan."},{"heading":"Rail timings for a four to six week visit","text":"A regular gap between sessions suits a fixed train or road trip. Check the timings and the return before you book the course. Winter fog can delay trains, so keep a spare date."},{"heading":"Reviews done locally","text":"Ask whether a Kanpur doctor can do a simple review if the plan is written down, and what the planning doctor needs to see afterwards. A review by video with photos in daylight may also be possible."},{"heading":"Dust and hard water","text":"Kanpur is an industrial city and people ask about dust and water and their hair. We make no claim that either causes hair thinning. Ask the doctor which shampoo suits your scalp. {pending}"}]'::jsonb, 'PRP Treatment in Kanpur: Cost, Sessions, Risks', 'PRP treatment in Kanpur', 'PRP treatment in Kanpur is a course of short visits every few weeks. The local sample cost per session is {tbc} until quotes are collected. No partner facility is confirmed in Kanpur yet, so the first question is whether sessions are local or in Lucknow, and whether reviews can be done near home.', '[{"heading":"Is it in Kanpur or in Lucknow","paragraphs":["That depends on whether a facility in Kanpur provides PRP, and none is confirmed yet. If the course is in Lucknow, each session is a day trip, and the plan should say how many trips there are and which of them are essential.","Ask whether the first session and a final review need to be in person, and whether the middle sessions can be done by a local doctor under the plan. Not every part of a course can be moved, and the doctor decides."]},{"heading":"Timing the gap between sessions","paragraphs":["In many plans the gap is around four to six weeks, and the reviewer will confirm a general range. That gap is easy to fit to a regular train or road trip, if the timings are checked. Put the dates on a calendar, and keep a spare date in case of winter fog or a delayed train.","A gap that stretches to months changes the plan, so ask the clinic what to do if you miss a date."]},{"heading":"Cold winters, hot summers and the scalp","paragraphs":["Kanpur has cold dry winters and hot summers, with dust and industrial air through the year. After a scalp session the doctor will say when to wash your hair and what to avoid. We make no claim that dust, heat or cold changes how PRP works.","In winter, hot water on a tender scalp can sting. In summer, sweat and dust are the concern. Ask what to do in the month you book."]},{"heading":"Water, shampoo and hair questions","paragraphs":["Water supply in the city mixes the river, piped supply and groundwater, and hardness differs by neighbourhood. People ask about hair and water. We make no claim that water causes hair thinning. Ask the doctor which shampoo suits your scalp and how often to wash."]},{"heading":"Referral, language and a second opinion","paragraphs":["Hindi and Hinglish are common in clinics. A family doctor can refer you and keep your notes, which helps if you see doctors in two cities. If hair thinning is the reason, ask whether thyroid, iron and hormone levels have been checked, and bring the reports.","If a person promises a result before a doctor has examined you, take that as a reason to ask for the plan in writing and a second opinion."]}]'::jsonb),
  ('hair-transplant', 'gurgaon', false, false, null, 'Hair transplant in Gurgaon (Gurugram): sample cost lines, how grafts and technique change the bill, recovery, risks and getting there from Delhi.', null, null, null, null, null, null, null, true, null, null, '{"surgeon":"varies","medicines":"varies","followups":"varies"}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"A partner facility exists in Gurgaon for other treatments, and whether it does hair transplants is to be confirmed. We do not name it. In this city a transplant is done in a day-care facility with a procedure room, so ask what kind of place you are in.","partners":[{"type":"Day-care facility in Gurgaon (to be confirmed)","count":null}],"accreditation":null,"checks":[{"check":"Registered doctor for key steps","why":"Who extracts and places grafts decides the result and the risk","ask":"Who performs extraction, site making and placement, and where can I check the registration?"},{"check":"Graft count in writing","why":"The bill is grafts times a rate, so the count must be written down","ask":"Can I have the graft number, how it is counted and the rate in writing?"},{"check":"Donor limits and reserve","why":"The donor area is limited and cannot be refilled","ask":"How much donor hair do I have, and how much is kept in reserve?"},{"check":"What is included","why":"Medicines, reviews and add-ons are often extra","ask":"What is included, what is extra, and what if growth is thin? Ask whether the doctor who plans the work is the doctor who performs it."},{"check":"Follow-up schedule","why":"A first wash and a review at about day 10 are common","ask":"Which reviews are in person, and can any be done near my home?"}]}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"Many people in Gurgaon work in offices and commute by car or two-wheeler. The questions here are same-day return or one night, how to ride home with a dressing, and where to do the follow-up if you return to Delhi.","airport":"Indira Gandhi International Airport, Delhi (to be verified)","station":"HUDA City Centre (Yellow Line) and Sikandarpur (Rapid Metro)","stayDays":"To be confirmed by the partner. From Delhi, many plans use a same-day return or one night","metro":"After a long day with a dressing, a booked cab is easier than a metro change, and walking to a station in the heat is not advised. {sample} The distance to a facility is added once one is confirmed.","roadTimes":[{"from":"South Delhi","time":"40 to 70 min","tip":"A late finish may meet the highway rush, so ask for an earlier start"},{"from":"Noida","time":"70 to 110 min","tip":"A one-night stay may be easier than a long ride at night"},{"from":"Faridabad","time":"60 to 100 min","tip":"Ask whether the first wash can be done locally"},{"from":"Rewari","time":"60 to 90 min","tip":"Ask whether a stay in Gurgaon is available for the first night"}],"privacyNote":"Many clients come from nearby offices. You do not need to explain the days off. Ask the clinic to keep the procedure name out of messages and reminders.","mapCaption":"Travel into Gurgaon from Delhi and nearby towns, no building shown."}'::jsonb, '[{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: whether the Gurgaon partner facility does hair transplants, and its type","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: groundwater hardness for Gurugram (Central Ground Water Board report, year)","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: whether a stay near the Gurgaon facility is available, and the follow-up arrangements","source":"","asOf":""}]'::jsonb, 'For people in Gurgaon (Gurugram) and those coming from Delhi who decide between a same-day return and one night, with notes on riding home with a dressing, a cap and helmet, follow-up in Delhi, and hard-water questions with no claim attached.', '{}'::jsonb, false, '[]'::jsonb, '["In Gurgaon the first decision is a same-day return or one night, and who rides you home.","A helmet or cap on a two-wheeler commute presses on grafts, so plan another way to travel.","Follow-up can be split between Gurgaon and Delhi if the plan is written down."]'::jsonb, null, '[{"heading":"Gurgaon or Gurugram","text":"They are the same city. This page uses Gurgaon because more people search for it, and the body text also says Gurugram. Either spelling works when you ask a clinic."},{"heading":"Same-day or one night from Delhi","text":"From South Delhi a same-day return is possible. From Noida or Faridabad, a night near the facility may be easier than a long ride in the dark. Ask what a stay costs and what it includes. {tbc}"},{"heading":"Helmet or cap on a two-wheeler","text":"A helmet presses on grafts, so do not ride a two-wheeler home or for the first weeks without asking the doctor. Arrange a cab and ask when a soft cap is allowed and when a helmet can be used again."},{"heading":"Gurgaon or Delhi for follow-up","text":"If you live in Delhi, ask whether the first wash and day 10 review can be done near home. A written plan and daylight photos can help a doctor elsewhere. Delhi is the nearest other city we cover."}]'::jsonb, 'Hair Transplant in Gurgaon: Cost, Recovery, Risks', 'Hair transplant in Gurgaon', 'The sample total for a hair transplant in Gurgaon (also written Gurugram) depends on grafts, technique and sessions. The procedure is done in a day-care facility, and the number of nights and follow-up visits is to be confirmed by the partner. A doctor checks the donor area before giving a graft number.', '[{"heading":"One long day and an office calendar","paragraphs":["A Gurgaon transplant takes most of a day, and then you have a dressing and a quiet first week. Check your work calendar before you set a date, and ask your employer about the days you need. Many people find it easiest to take the procedure on a Thursday or Friday and use the weekend to rest.","Plan the first wash and the review at about day 10 into the same calendar. A few meetings by video from home in the second week are usually easier than meetings in a crowded office."]},{"heading":"Heat, air conditioning and a healing scalp","paragraphs":["Gurgaon summers run from April into September, with heat and sweat, and air-conditioned offices dry the skin. After a transplant, sweat and sports are usually limited for a period, so a summer date may be harder. Ask the doctor how the month you pick changes the advice.","We make no claim that heat or air conditioning changes how grafts grow."]},{"heading":"Hard water, shampoo and the wash routine","paragraphs":["Groundwater in parts of Gurugram is described as hard or salty, and many people ask whether it affects a healing scalp. We make no claim about that and no source is attached yet. Ask the doctor how to wash after the procedure, which water to use and which shampoo suits your scalp."]},{"heading":"Referral habits and asking a second doctor","paragraphs":["People often get a clinic name from a colleague. A name is a place to start, and not a check. Ask for the registration of the doctor who performs the key steps, the written graft number and what is included. A second opinion from a dermatologist you already see is a good step.","Be careful of a package sold on the first call, and of a graft number given before the doctor has seen your scalp."]},{"heading":"Monsoon and travel delays","paragraphs":["Heavy rain can cause long delays in July and August. Leave a buffer for the return after the procedure and for the first wash visit. If rain stops you from reaching the clinic, call and ask what to do, and do not skip the wash routine."]}]'::jsonb),
  ('hair-transplant', 'delhi', false, false, null, 'Hair transplant in Delhi: sample cost lines, how grafts and technique change the bill, recovery, risks, and how to reach Delhi from nearby towns.', null, null, null, null, null, null, null, true, null, null, '{"surgeon":"varies","medicines":"varies","followups":"varies"}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"No partner facility is confirmed in Delhi yet. A hair transplant is done in a day-care facility with a procedure room, and not on a hospital ward. This page will name the facility type once one is confirmed. Until then, use the questions below on any place you are considering.","partners":[{"type":"Day-care facility in Delhi (to be confirmed)","count":null}],"accreditation":null,"checks":[{"check":"Registered doctor for key steps","why":"Who extracts and places grafts decides the result and the risk","ask":"Who performs extraction, site making and placement, and where can I check the registration?"},{"check":"Graft count in writing","why":"The bill is grafts times a rate, so the count must be written down","ask":"Can I have the graft number, how it is counted and the rate in writing?"},{"check":"Donor limits and reserve","why":"The donor area is limited and cannot be refilled","ask":"How much donor hair do I have, and how much is kept in reserve?"},{"check":"What is included","why":"Medicines, reviews and add-ons are often extra","ask":"What is included, what is extra, and what if growth is thin? Ask about parking and attendant rules on the day."},{"check":"Follow-up schedule","why":"A first wash and a review at about day 10 are common","ask":"Which reviews are in person, and can any be done near my home?"}]}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"A transplant is a long day with a dressing at the end, and then a first wash visit and a review. The questions in Delhi are how to travel home after the day, whether to stay near the facility, and how smog and heat affect a healing scalp.","airport":"Indira Gandhi International Airport (to be verified)","station":"New Delhi, Old Delhi and Hazrat Nizamuddin stations (to be verified against the facility)","stayDays":"To be confirmed by the partner. Many plans use a same-day return or one night","metro":"After a long day with a dressing, a cab with an attendant is easier than the metro, and rush hours can be slow. {sample} Whether a nearby stay is available is added once a facility is confirmed.","roadTimes":[{"from":"Noida","time":"50 to 90 min","tip":"A same-night return is possible, and the first wash visit is a second trip"},{"from":"Ghaziabad","time":"60 to 100 min","tip":"Ask whether the first wash can be done by a local doctor"},{"from":"Faridabad","time":"50 to 90 min","tip":"Plan the return for a time away from peak traffic"},{"from":"Gurgaon","time":"50 to 90 min","tip":"Compare Gurgaon facilities before you commit"}],"privacyNote":"A cap and a loose scarf can cover a dressing on the way home. Photos of your scalp are health data, so ask where clinic photos are stored and who can see them.","mapCaption":"Travel into Delhi from nearby towns, no building shown."}'::jsonb, '[{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: which Delhi facility, if any, will do hair transplants, and its type","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: winter and post-Diwali air quality in Delhi (public CPCB records, month and station)","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: parking and attendant rules at the partner facility","source":"","asOf":""}]'::jsonb, 'For readers in Delhi and nearby NCR towns who plan one long day for a transplant, with notes on the ride home with a dressing, whether to stay a night, smog and a healing scalp, and parking and attendant rules.', '{}'::jsonb, false, '[]'::jsonb, '["A transplant in Delhi is one long day, so the ride home with a dressing is part of the plan.","Smog and a fresh transplant is a question to put to the doctor, who may advise staying indoors.","Parking and attendant rules differ between facilities, so ask before the day."]'::jsonb, null, '[{"heading":"Travelling home after the day","text":"You leave with a dressing and tender scalp. Arrange a cab or a driver, and bring someone with you. Avoid a crowded metro car, where a head can be bumped, and a two-wheeler is not advised."},{"heading":"Is a stay needed","text":"Many people return home the same night, and some stay one night near the facility. If you live more than an hour away, ask whether a stay is available, and what it costs. {tbc}"},{"heading":"Smog and a fresh transplant","text":"Poor air in winter, and after Diwali in particular, raises the question of going out in the first days. We make no claim about what smog does to grafts. Ask the doctor what to do, and plan the date with the season in mind. {pending}"},{"heading":"Parking and attendant rules","text":"Some facilities limit who may enter with you. Ask whether an attendant can stay in the facility, where the driver can wait, and what the visiting hours are on the day."}]'::jsonb, 'Hair Transplant in Delhi: Cost, Recovery, Risks', 'Hair transplant in Delhi', 'The sample total for a hair transplant in Delhi depends on grafts, technique and sessions. In Delhi the procedure is done in a day-care facility, and the number of nights and follow-up visits is to be confirmed by the partner. A doctor checks the donor area before giving a graft number.', '[{"heading":"A long day, planned from the end","paragraphs":["Plan a Delhi transplant from the ride home backwards. The procedure takes most of a day, you finish with a dressing and a tender scalp, and the road from the facility to your door may take an hour or more. Fix the cab, the attendant and the first-night bed before you book the date.","Ask the clinic at what time the procedure usually ends, so that your return does not fall in the evening rush. If the ride is long, ask whether a stay nearby is possible."]},{"heading":"Air quality, dust and the first week","paragraphs":["Delhi has long spells of poor air in winter, and dust and heat in summer. A healing scalp is sensitive, so the doctor may advise staying indoors for the first days and covering the head when you go out. We make no claim about what pollution does to grafts.","If you can choose the month, ask the doctor how the season changes the plan. A date in a stretch of very poor air, or in the hottest weeks, may be harder to manage."]},{"heading":"Reviews: what must be in person","paragraphs":["A first wash is often planned for the next day and a review around day 10. Ask which of these must be at the facility. If you live in Noida, Ghaziabad or Faridabad, a local doctor may do a simple check if the plan is written down, and a photo review may fill other gaps.","Later reviews are usually spaced over months. Photos in daylight help the doctor see growth from far away."]},{"heading":"Language and the written plan","paragraphs":["Staff at most Delhi clinics speak Hindi and English, and some speak Punjabi. Ask for the graft number, the method and the aftercare written in the language you read most easily. Compare plans for the same graft number and method. {tbc}"]},{"heading":"Timing around weddings and work","paragraphs":["Scabs and redness last about two weeks and shedding follows. If you have a wedding or a big event, plan the procedure at least a few months ahead, and do not book the week before. Ask your employer about leave for the first days and the reviews."]}]'::jsonb),
  ('hair-transplant', 'lucknow', false, false, null, 'Hair transplant in Lucknow: sample cost lines, how grafts and technique change the bill, recovery, risks, and how to reach Lucknow from nearby towns.', null, null, null, null, null, null, null, true, null, null, '{"surgeon":"varies","medicines":"varies","followups":"varies"}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"No partner facility is confirmed in Lucknow yet. A transplant is done in a day-care facility with a procedure room. If care ends up in another city, we will say so at the top of this page and not claim a local site.","partners":[{"type":"Day-care facility in Lucknow (to be confirmed)","count":null}],"accreditation":null,"checks":[{"check":"Registered doctor for key steps","why":"Who extracts and places grafts decides the result and the risk","ask":"Who performs extraction, site making and placement, and where can I check the registration?"},{"check":"Graft count in writing","why":"The bill is grafts times a rate, so the count must be written down","ask":"Can I have the graft number, how it is counted and the rate in writing?"},{"check":"Donor limits and reserve","why":"The donor area is limited and cannot be refilled","ask":"How much donor hair do I have, and how much is kept in reserve?"},{"check":"What is included","why":"Medicines, reviews and add-ons are often extra","ask":"What is included, what is extra, and what if growth is thin? From a nearby town, ask where you get your first wash done."},{"check":"Follow-up schedule","why":"A first wash and a review at about day 10 are common","ask":"Which reviews are in person, and can any be done near my home?"}]}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"For many people the trip is the hard part. You come from a district town, spend a long day at the facility, and then need to sleep somewhere before the first wash and the ride home.","airport":"Chaudhary Charan Singh International Airport, Lucknow (to be verified)","station":"Charbagh station and the Lucknow Metro (to be verified against the facility)","stayDays":"To be confirmed by the partner. From a district town, plan one or two nights","metro":"The Lucknow Metro runs along a north-south line and can help for the consultation. After the procedure, a booked cab to your stay is easier. {sample} A stay near the facility is added once one is confirmed.","roadTimes":[{"from":"Barabanki","time":"40 to 70 min","tip":"A same-day return is possible, and the first wash is a second trip"},{"from":"Unnao","time":"60 to 100 min","tip":"A night near the facility may be easier than a late drive"},{"from":"Sitapur","time":"80 to 120 min","tip":"Plan one night, and ask where the first wash can be done"},{"from":"Hardoi","time":"100 to 150 min","tip":"Plan two nights, and ask which reviews can be by video"}],"privacyNote":"In a smaller town a neighbour may notice a dressing. A cap on the way home helps, and a clinic should keep the procedure name out of messages.","mapCaption":"Travel into Lucknow from nearby districts, no building shown."}'::jsonb, '[{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: which Lucknow facility, if any, will do hair transplants, and its type","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: availability and cost of a stay near the facility, and the first wash arrangement","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: Lucknow climate normals for heat, dust and humidity (IMD) and Gomti water supply hardness","source":"","asOf":""}]'::jsonb, 'For readers in Lucknow and nearby districts who come for a day-care procedure and need to plan a night or two, with notes on where to get the first wash, summer sweat rules, a Hindi-speaking coordinator and reviews by video.', '{}'::jsonb, false, '[]'::jsonb, '["From a district town, a transplant is a day at the facility plus a night or two, so the stay is part of the plan.","The first wash is the visit people forget to plan, and it must be somewhere you can reach.","Summer sweat and dust shape the advice for the first weeks."]'::jsonb, null, '[{"heading":"Coming from a small town","text":"A day-care procedure is one long day. You arrive early, finish in the afternoon or evening and need somewhere to sleep. Bring a family member, and plan the ride home for the day after the first wash."},{"heading":"A night near the facility","text":"Ask whether a stay is available and what it costs, or look for a place close to the facility so that you are not on the road at night. {tbc}"},{"heading":"Where to get the first wash","text":"The first wash is usually the next day. If you leave on the same night, ask who will do it, how, and what to use. A local doctor can do it if the plan is written down, and the doctor who did the procedure may want a photo."},{"heading":"Summer sweat rules","text":"Lucknow summers are hot, and sweat and dust are limited for a period after a transplant. Ask what to do on a day in May or June, and whether the month you picked makes things harder."}]'::jsonb, 'Hair Transplant in Lucknow: Cost, Recovery, Risks', 'Hair transplant in Lucknow', 'The sample total for a hair transplant in Lucknow depends on grafts, technique and sessions. Many people come from nearby towns for a day-care procedure and need a place to stay. The number of nights and follow-up visits is to be confirmed by the partner. A doctor checks the donor area before giving a graft number.', '[{"heading":"A long day and a night away","paragraphs":["For most people from Sitapur, Hardoi or Unnao, a transplant is not a day trip. The procedure runs from morning into the afternoon, you leave with a dressing, and the road home after dark is tiring. A night near the facility, and a first wash the next morning, make the plan easier.","Ask the clinic for the full timeline: arrival time, likely finish, the wash visit, and the earliest sensible time to travel home. Put the dates on a calendar and check them against work, farming seasons, festivals and exams."]},{"heading":"Dust, summer heat and monsoon","paragraphs":["Lucknow summers are hot and dry, with dust, and the monsoon is humid. A healing scalp needs care in both. The doctor will say how long to avoid sweat and sun, and what to wear outdoors. Ask what to do on the first days in your month.","We make no claim that dust or humidity changes how grafts grow. If your scalp is sore or you see pus, call the clinic."]},{"heading":"Water and the wash routine","paragraphs":["Households use a mix of piped supply and groundwater, and hardness varies by area. People ask whether water affects a healing scalp, and we make no claim about that. Ask the doctor how to wash, which water and shampoo to use and how often."]},{"heading":"Referrals from a local doctor","paragraphs":["In smaller towns, many people hear about hair transplants from a local doctor, a barber, a pharmacist or a relative. Ask a doctor you trust whether you are a candidate, and whether your thyroid, iron and hormone levels have been checked. Bring any reports.","Be careful of a phone call or a message that quotes a graft number and a price before a doctor has seen your scalp. Ask for the registration of the doctor who performs the key steps."]},{"heading":"Language, festivals and fog","paragraphs":["Hindi and Hinglish are common in clinics, and you can ask for the plan and the aftercare in the language you read most easily. Festivals, weddings and winter fog change roads and trains, so keep a spare date for the review and a buffer for the return."]}]'::jsonb),
  ('hair-transplant', 'kanpur', false, false, null, 'Hair transplant in Kanpur: sample cost lines, how grafts and technique change the bill, recovery, risks, and how to reach the facility from nearby towns.', null, null, null, null, null, null, null, true, null, null, '{"surgeon":"varies","medicines":"varies","followups":"varies"}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"No partner facility is confirmed in Kanpur, and Lucknow is the nearest other city we cover. If a transplant is done in Lucknow, we will say so at the top of this page, with the trip time. Until then, this page shows how to plan and what to check.","partners":[{"type":"Day-care facility in Kanpur (to be confirmed)","count":null}],"accreditation":null,"checks":[{"check":"Registered doctor for key steps","why":"Who extracts and places grafts decides the result and the risk","ask":"Who performs extraction, site making and placement, and where can I check the registration?"},{"check":"Graft count in writing","why":"The bill is grafts times a rate, so the count must be written down","ask":"Can I have the graft number, how it is counted and the rate in writing?"},{"check":"Donor limits and reserve","why":"The donor area is limited and cannot be refilled","ask":"How much donor hair do I have, and how much is kept in reserve?"},{"check":"What is included","why":"Medicines, reviews and add-ons are often extra","ask":"What is included, what is extra, and what if growth is thin? If the procedure is in Lucknow, ask which reviews must be there."},{"check":"Follow-up schedule","why":"A first wash and a review at about day 10 are common","ask":"Which reviews are in person, and can any be done near my home?"}]}'::jsonb, '{"intro":"For Kanpur the main question is which city does the procedure. If it is Lucknow, you travel for the day, return with a dressing and then plan the follow-up from Kanpur.","airport":"Kanpur civil airport and Lucknow airport (service and schedules to be verified)","station":"Kanpur Central, and Charbagh in Lucknow (to be verified)","stayDays":"To be confirmed. If the procedure is in Lucknow, plan a night there, or a long return the same day","metro":"Kanpur has a metro line that is partly open, and the part open is to be checked against any facility. {sample} After a procedure, a cab is easier than a crowded train.","roadTimes":[{"from":"Unnao","time":"30 to 60 min","tip":"Close enough for a same-day return if the finish is early"},{"from":"Kanpur Dehat","time":"40 to 80 min","tip":"Plan the return for daylight"},{"from":"Fatehpur","time":"70 to 110 min","tip":"A night in the city may be easier than a late road"},{"from":"Lucknow","time":"100 to 150 min","tip":"The other city we cover. Check the road and train times in current sources"}],"privacyNote":"In a mid-sized city many people know each other. You do not have to explain a dressing, and a clinic should keep the procedure name out of messages.","mapCaption":"Travel into Kanpur from nearby towns, and the road to Lucknow, no building shown."}'::jsonb, '[{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: which Kanpur or Lucknow facility will do the procedure, and its type","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: Kanpur to Lucknow road time and expressway status, and the rail timetable, with a date","source":"","asOf":""},{"text":"NEEDS REAL DATA: Kanpur air quality record (public CPCB station data) and groundwater hardness","source":"","asOf":""}]'::jsonb, 'For readers in Kanpur and nearby towns who must decide where the procedure takes place and how follow-up works after they return, with notes on the road to Lucknow, helmet use after a transplant, local reviews and dust and hard-water questions without a claim.', '{}'::jsonb, false, '[]'::jsonb, '["In Kanpur the first question is which city does the procedure, and the second is who follows up at home.","A helmet on a two-wheeler is a real question after a transplant and needs a plan for the first weeks.","Follow-up near home is possible only if the written plan reaches a Kanpur doctor."]'::jsonb, null, '[{"heading":"Which facility does the procedure","text":"A facility in Kanpur or one in Lucknow may do the procedure, and none is confirmed yet. Ask where the doctor works and where the procedure takes place, and how long the trip is from your home."},{"heading":"Follow-up after returning to Kanpur","text":"You may be back in Kanpur for the first wash and the review at about day 10. Ask whether a Kanpur doctor can do a simple check from a written plan, and what the planning doctor needs to see."},{"heading":"Helmet use after a transplant","text":"A helmet presses on grafts. Ask when you can ride a two-wheeler again with one, and what to use in the meantime. Arrange a car or a cab for the ride home and the early reviews."},{"heading":"Dust and hard water","text":"Kanpur is an industrial city, and people ask about dust and water and a healing scalp. We make no claim that either affects grafts. Ask the doctor how to wash and which shampoo suits your scalp. {pending}"}]'::jsonb, 'Hair Transplant in Kanpur: Cost, Recovery, Risks', 'Hair transplant in Kanpur', 'The sample total for a hair transplant in Kanpur depends on grafts, technique and sessions. No partner facility is confirmed in Kanpur yet, so the first question is whether the procedure is done in Kanpur or in Lucknow, and what follow-up can be done near home. A doctor checks the donor area before giving a graft number.', '[{"heading":"Kanpur or Lucknow for the procedure","paragraphs":["That depends on whether a facility in Kanpur does hair transplants, and none is confirmed yet. If the procedure is in Lucknow, it is a long day, with a night in the city, and a ride home with a dressing.","Ask the clinic how long the procedure takes, when you will finish and what the earliest sensible time to travel is. If the road or train time is long, plan a night and travel the next day after the first wash."]},{"heading":"Planning the follow-up from home","paragraphs":["After the procedure, the first wash comes the next day and a review about ten days later, with later reviews over many months. Ask which of these must be with the doctor who did the work and which can be done in Kanpur.","A written plan, daylight photos at set dates and a named person to reach at the clinic help a lot. If a problem shows up between reviews, you need a name to call."]},{"heading":"Cold winters, hot summers and dust","paragraphs":["Kanpur has cold dry winters and hot summers, with dust and industrial air through the year. A healing scalp needs care in each. In winter, very hot water can sting, and in summer, sweat and sun are the concern. The doctor will say what to avoid, and for how long.","We make no claim that dust, heat or cold changes how grafts grow."]},{"heading":"Water, shampoo and wash advice","paragraphs":["Water supply in the city mixes the river, piped supply and groundwater, and hardness differs by neighbourhood. People ask about water and a healing scalp. We make no claim about it. Ask the doctor how to wash, and which shampoo suits you."]},{"heading":"Referral, language and a second opinion","paragraphs":["Hindi and Hinglish are common in clinics. A family doctor can refer you and keep your notes, which helps if you see doctors in two cities. Ask whether thyroid, iron and hormone levels have been checked, and bring the reports.","If a person promises a result before a doctor has examined you, ask for the plan in writing and take a second opinion."]}]'::jsonb)
